{"type":"message","id":"4233e1f2","parentId":"2a12b3e4","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:35:37.074Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture:\n\n1. The cron job successfully ran at 11:00 (10:46 actually, because of the update delay) with xixi as the agent and MiniMax-M2.7 model - status \"ok\"\n2. But the model was MiniMax-M2.7, NOT arkcode/glm-4.7 as requested. This is odd.\n\nWait, looking at the runs more carefully:\n- First entry (most recent): `model: \"MiniMax-M2.7\"`, `provider: \"minimax\"` - this is the 11:00 run with xixi\n- But we updated the cron to use arkcode/glm-4.7 at ~10:46\n\n\n- The 11:00 run completed in 152 seconds with 140K input tokens, so xixi is clearly doing real work here, but the model choice doesn't match what was configured\n\nLooking at the project file, there are an overwhelming number of issues being tracked - 145+ with most in \"newly discovered\" status. The file has ballooned significantly since the last update.\n\nThe real concern is that the scan found something actionable at 11:00 but there's no evidence it's been worked on - xixi just marked it as \"scanning complete\" and tried to report back to main, but the cron delivery failed. Meanwhile, P44 (#55995) and P45 (#55994) haven't progressed beyond discovery despite being critical security and regression issues. The agents seem to be stuck in a loop of scanning and cataloging without actually resolving anything.\n\nI'm realizing the cron runs successfully and xixi is identifying real problems - that's working as intended. But the issue is that xixi doesn't have the agency to actually test hypotheses or drive issues to completion; it can only research and document. The architectural gap is that there's no follow-through mechanism where scan findings lead to actual fixes or PR submissions.\n\nBeyond that, the sheer volume of findings - over 145 tracked items - suggests the bar for what counts as actionable is too low. And chronologically, something doesn't add up: the cron ran at 10:46 but the model was MiniMax-M2.7, not the glm-4.7 that should have been used based on the timestamp.","thinkingSignature":"2b30a0652311d2f4cd51541649d53f13fbdf91f0a3eafeaff8619a751e1d74bf"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_bm5la21p683p_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron list 2>&1 | grep -A3 \"6f8bd6c8\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":31893,"output":515,"cacheRead":22915,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55323,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774672519453}}
