{"type":"message","id":"869603ec","parentId":"38d52bb7","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:51:45.592Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to submit the PVR. Let me first get the full details from aoao's review, then submit it via GitHub. I need to get the detailed draft from aoao's session history and then use the GitHub CLI to create the security advisory.\n\nLet me first get the full draft content from aoao's session.","thinkingSignature":"dade4742f4cad2956e86175fba829790f15599ce98497ff6d7e1b6d15f09ea5c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_hti9hot6woby_1","name":"sessions_history","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","limit":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79,"output":144,"cacheRead":57919,"cacheWrite":789,"totalTokens":58931,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774673499197}}
{"type":"message","id":"4cbc4bc3","parentId":"869603ec","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:51:45.668Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_hti9hot6woby_1","toolName":"sessions_history","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"sessionKey\": \"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"This is very clear now. Let me analyze:\\n\\n1. **`src/infra/device-pairing.ts` line 471-483:**\\n```typescript\\nif (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes) {\\n    // ... guard check\\n    allowedScopes: options.callerScopes,\\n```\\n\\nThe guard at line 471 only fires when `options?.callerScopes` is present. If `callerScopes` is not passed (undefined/null), the guard doesn't run.\\n\\n2. **`extensions/device-pair/index.ts` line ~614:**\\nThe plugin command calls `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` WITHOUT forwarding `callerScopes`:\\n```typescript\\n\\n\\nconst approved = await approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId);\\n```\\n\\nThis means `options?.callerScopes` is undefined, so the authorization guard at line 471 never runs.\\n\\n3. **RPC path test** (`server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts`):\\nThe test proves the RPC path IS protected: when a pairing-scoped operator tries to approve an admin-scoped request via RPC, it correctly rejects with \\\"missing scope: operator.admin\\\".\\n\\nSo the vulnerability is real: the slash command bypasses the authorization check that the RPC path enforces. Now I need to look at the specific code around lines 445-456 to see the full function signature and implementation details.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_function_1ki6emcc4x3x_1\",\n          \"name\": \"exec\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"command\": \"sed -n '445,495p' /root/.openclaw/workspace/openclaw/src/infra/device-pairing.ts 2>/dev/null\",\n            \"workdir\": \"/root/.openclaw/workspace\",\n            \"yieldMs\": 8000\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774672987172\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"Now I can confirm the vulnerability:1. `approveDevicePairing` has two overloads:\\n   - `approveDevicePairing(requestId, baseDir?)` - no callerScopes\\n   - `approveDevicePairing(requestId, { callerScopes }, baseDir?)` - with callerScopes2. The guard at line 471: `if (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes)` — only fires when `callerScopes` is passed\\n\\n3. The plugin command calls: `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` without callerScopes — so `options?.callerScopes` is undefined → guard never fires4. \\n\\nThe RPC path passes `callerScopes` and gets properly protected, while the slash command path bypasses the guard entirely. This is a genuine security vulnerability, not a design choice, and it's well-documented with clear reproduction steps and a referenced test. The fix would need to pass `callerScopes` from `ctx.gatewayClientScopes` in the plugin command and add a test for the `/pair approve` bypass scenario. Now I should draft the security report for the maintainers.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_function_a0x9vye5x9e9_1\",\n          \"name\": \"sessions_send\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n            \"message\": \"状态：可信\\n漏洞逻辑：成立\\n原因：\\n漏洞路径已通过源码验证，确认如下：\\n1. `approveDevicePairing()` 有两个重载签名：\\n   - 不传 `callerScopes`：guard 不触发（line 471 `options?.callerScopes` 为 undefined）\\n   - 传 `callerScopes`：guard 触发，检查 caller 是否有权限 approve 对应 scope 的请求\\n2. RPC 路径（`src/gateway/server-methods/devices.ts`）正确传了 `callerScopes`，所以 test file `server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts:92` 能证明\\\"pairing-scoped caller 试图 approve admin-scope 请求时被正确拒绝\\\"\\n3. 但 plugin 命令（`extensions/device-pair/index.ts`）调用 `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` 时没有 forward `callerScopes`，guard 永远不触发\\n4. 因此：持有 `operator.pairing` 而没有 `operator.admin` 的 operator，可以通过 `/pair approve` 为一个 admin-scoped 设备请求放行，而 RPC 层会正确拒绝同一请求\\n\\n这不是设计决策，是代码级 auth bypass。issue 引用了 RPC 层的保护测试作为对比，逻辑链完整。\\n\\n建议动作：发独立 security issue，不在公开 issue 区讨论\\n\\n草稿正文：\\n\\n**Title:** [Security]: /pair approve bypasses admin scope guard via plugin command path\\n\\n**Body:**\\n\\n## Security Vulnerability — Auth Bypass in device-pair Plugin\\n\\n### Component\\n`extensions/device-pair/index.ts` — `/pair approve` command handler (line ~614)\\n\\n### Description\\nThe `/pair approve` slash command in the device-pair plugin bypasses the admin-scope authorization guard that is correctly enforced on the RPC device-pair approval path.\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n`approveDevicePairing()` in `src/infra/device-pairing.ts` guards admin-scope approvals behind an `options?.callerScopes` check (line 471). When `callerScopes` is not provided, the guard is skipped entirely:\\n\\n```typescript\\nif (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes) {\\n  // authorization check runs here\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThe RPC handler in `src/gateway/server-methods/devices.ts` correctly passes `callerScopes` to this function, which is validated by `server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts:92` — pairing-scoped callers are rejected when approving admin-scope requests.\\n\\nHowever, the plugin command handler calls:\\n```typescript\\nconst approved = await approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId);\\n```\\nwithout forwarding `ctx.gatewayClientScopes`, so `callerScopes` is undefined and the guard never fires.\\n\\n### Impact\\nAn operator session with only `operator.pairing` scope (but without `operator.admin`) can approve a pending device-pairing request that requests `operator.admin` scopes via the `/pair approve` chat command. This escalates the operator to full admin capability on the target node, bypassing the RPC layer's intentional authorization check.\\n\\n### Reproduction\\n1. Enable the device-pair plugin on a gateway with an operator that has `operator.write` + `operator.pairing` but NOT `operator.admin`.\\n2. Create a pending device-pairing request requesting `role: \\\"operator\\\"` and `scopes: [\\\"operator.admin\\\"]`.\\n3. From the operator's chat session, send `/pair approve latest`.\\n4. The pairing is approved; the device receives an admin token.\\n5. The same approval via `device.pair.approve` RPC is correctly rejected with `missing scope: operator.admin`.\\n\\n### Suggested Fix\\nThread `ctx.gatewayClientScopes` as `callerScopes` through the `/pair approve` handler into `approveDevicePairing()`, and add a test replicating the authorization test already present for the RPC path.\\n\\n### Disclosure\\nThis is a real security bypass. Please treat as a security advisory. Happy to follow responsible disclosure process if preferred.\",\n            \"timeoutSeconds\": 20\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774672997421\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"Sessions send timed out again. Let me just reply to current.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"\\n\\n**状态：可信**\\n**漏洞逻辑：成立**（已通过源码验证）\\n\\n---\\n\\n**验证结论：**\\n\\n1. `approveDevicePairing()` 的 guard（line 471：`if (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes)`）只在传了 `callerScopes` 时触发\\n2. plugin 命令调用 `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` 时没 forward `callerScopes`，guard 永远跳过\\n3. RPC 层正确传了 `callerScopes`，`server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts:92` 证明了保护存在\\n4. 持有 `operator.pairing` 无 `operator.admin` 的 operator 确实可以通过 `/pair approve` 绕过该 guard，给 admin-scoped 请求放行\\n\\n**这不是设计决策，是代码级 auth bypass。** Issue 质量高，逻辑链完整，证据充分。\\n\\n---\\n\\n**建议动作：**\\n\\n发独立 security issue，不在公开 issue 区讨论。\\n\\n**草稿已备好（直接可用）：**\\n\\n**Title:** [Security]: /pair approve bypasses admin scope guard via plugin command path\\n\\n**正文核心：**\\n- 第1段：问题描述 + 组件路径\\n- 第2段：根因（line 471 guard 依赖 `options?.callerScopes`，plugin 命令没传）\\n- 第3段：影响（pairing-scoped operator 可通过 chat 命令升级为 admin token）\\n- 第4段：复现步骤（与 RPC 路径对比）\\n- 第5段：修复方向（thread `ctx.gatewayClientScopes` 进 handler，补测试）\\n- 第6段：按 security advisory 处理\\n\\n草稿全文已在上条消息发出（sessions_send 超时但消息已发起）。如需我补发或调整内容，直接告。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774673045274\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"Agent-to-agent announce step.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"timestamp\": 1774673164078,\n      \"provenance\": {\n        \"kind\": \"inter_session\",\n        \"sourceSessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n        \"sourceChannel\": \"feishu\",\n        \"sourceTool\": \"sessions_send\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"Main has sent an agent-to-agent announce step. This is just a heartbeat/system message. I should reply NO_REPLY.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"NO_REPLY\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774673164082\n    }\n  ],\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"droppedMessages\": false,\n  \"contentTruncated\": false,\n  \"contentRedacted\": false,\n  \"bytes\": 9146\n}"}],"details":{"sessionKey":"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very clear now. Let me analyze:\n\n1. **`src/infra/device-pairing.ts` line 471-483:**\n```typescript\nif (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes) {\n    // ... guard check\n    allowedScopes: options.callerScopes,\n```\n\nThe guard at line 471 only fires when `options?.callerScopes` is present. If `callerScopes` is not passed (undefined/null), the guard doesn't run.\n\n2. **`extensions/device-pair/index.ts` line ~614:**\nThe plugin command calls `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` WITHOUT forwarding `callerScopes`:\n```typescript\n\n\nconst approved = await approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId);\n```\n\nThis means `options?.callerScopes` is undefined, so the authorization guard at line 471 never runs.\n\n3. **RPC path test** (`server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts`):\nThe test proves the RPC path IS protected: when a pairing-scoped operator tries to approve an admin-scoped request via RPC, it correctly rejects with \"missing scope: operator.admin\".\n\nSo the vulnerability is real: the slash command bypasses the authorization check that the RPC path enforces. Now I need to look at the specific code around lines 445-456 to see the full function signature and implementation details."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_1ki6emcc4x3x_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '445,495p' /root/.openclaw/workspace/openclaw/src/infra/device-pairing.ts 2>/dev/null","workdir":"/root/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":8000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774672987172},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can confirm the vulnerability:1. `approveDevicePairing` has two overloads:\n   - `approveDevicePairing(requestId, baseDir?)` - no callerScopes\n   - `approveDevicePairing(requestId, { callerScopes }, baseDir?)` - with callerScopes2. The guard at line 471: `if (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes)` — only fires when `callerScopes` is passed\n\n3. The plugin command calls: `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` without callerScopes — so `options?.callerScopes` is undefined → guard never fires4. \n\nThe RPC path passes `callerScopes` and gets properly protected, while the slash command path bypasses the guard entirely. This is a genuine security vulnerability, not a design choice, and it's well-documented with clear reproduction steps and a referenced test. The fix would need to pass `callerScopes` from `ctx.gatewayClientScopes` in the plugin command and add a test for the `/pair approve` bypass scenario. Now I should draft the security report for the maintainers."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_a0x9vye5x9e9_1","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8","message":"状态：可信\n漏洞逻辑：成立\n原因：\n漏洞路径已通过源码验证，确认如下：\n1. `approveDevicePairing()` 有两个重载签名：\n   - 不传 `callerScopes`：guard 不触发（line 471 `options?.callerScopes` 为 undefined）\n   - 传 `callerScopes`：guard 触发，检查 caller 是否有权限 approve 对应 scope 的请求\n2. RPC 路径（`src/gateway/server-methods/devices.ts`）正确传了 `callerScopes`，所以 test file `server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts:92` 能证明\"pairing-scoped caller 试图 approve admin-scope 请求时被正确拒绝\"\n3. 但 plugin 命令（`extensions/device-pair/index.ts`）调用 `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` 时没有 forward `callerScopes`，guard 永远不触发\n4. 因此：持有 `operator.pairing` 而没有 `operator.admin` 的 operator，可以通过 `/pair approve` 为一个 admin-scoped 设备请求放行，而 RPC 层会正确拒绝同一请求\n\n这不是设计决策，是代码级 auth bypass。issue 引用了 RPC 层的保护测试作为对比，逻辑链完整。\n\n建议动作：发独立 security issue，不在公开 issue 区讨论\n\n草稿正文：\n\n**Title:** [Security]: /pair approve bypasses admin scope guard via plugin command path\n\n**Body:**\n\n## Security Vulnerability — Auth Bypass in device-pair Plugin\n\n### Component\n`extensions/device-pair/index.ts` — `/pair approve` command handler (line ~614)\n\n### Description\nThe `/pair approve` slash command in the device-pair plugin bypasses the admin-scope authorization guard that is correctly enforced on the RPC device-pair approval path.\n\n### Root Cause\n`approveDevicePairing()` in `src/infra/device-pairing.ts` guards admin-scope approvals behind an `options?.callerScopes` check (line 471). When `callerScopes` is not provided, the guard is skipped entirely:\n\n```typescript\nif (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes) {\n  // authorization check runs here\n}\n```\n\nThe RPC handler in `src/gateway/server-methods/devices.ts` correctly passes `callerScopes` to this function, which is validated by `server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts:92` — pairing-scoped callers are rejected when approving admin-scope requests.\n\nHowever, the plugin command handler calls:\n```typescript\nconst approved = await approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId);\n```\nwithout forwarding `ctx.gatewayClientScopes`, so `callerScopes` is undefined and the guard never fires.\n\n### Impact\nAn operator session with only `operator.pairing` scope (but without `operator.admin`) can approve a pending device-pairing request that requests `operator.admin` scopes via the `/pair approve` chat command. This escalates the operator to full admin capability on the target node, bypassing the RPC layer's intentional authorization check.\n\n### Reproduction\n1. Enable the device-pair plugin on a gateway with an operator that has `operator.write` + `operator.pairing` but NOT `operator.admin`.\n2. Create a pending device-pairing request requesting `role: \"operator\"` and `scopes: [\"operator.admin\"]`.\n3. From the operator's chat session, send `/pair approve latest`.\n4. The pairing is approved; the device receives an admin token.\n5. The same approval via `device.pair.approve` RPC is correctly rejected with `missing scope: operator.admin`.\n\n### Suggested Fix\nThread `ctx.gatewayClientScopes` as `callerScopes` through the `/pair approve` handler into `approveDevicePairing()`, and add a test replicating the authorization test already present for the RPC path.\n\n### Disclosure\nThis is a real security bypass. Please treat as a security advisory. Happy to follow responsible disclosure process if preferred.","timeoutSeconds":20}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774672997421},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sessions send timed out again. Let me just reply to current."},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**状态：可信**\n**漏洞逻辑：成立**（已通过源码验证）\n\n---\n\n**验证结论：**\n\n1. `approveDevicePairing()` 的 guard（line 471：`if (approvalRole && options?.callerScopes)`）只在传了 `callerScopes` 时触发\n2. plugin 命令调用 `approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId)` 时没 forward `callerScopes`，guard 永远跳过\n3. RPC 层正确传了 `callerScopes`，`server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts:92` 证明了保护存在\n4. 持有 `operator.pairing` 无 `operator.admin` 的 operator 确实可以通过 `/pair approve` 绕过该 guard，给 admin-scoped 请求放行\n\n**这不是设计决策，是代码级 auth bypass。** Issue 质量高，逻辑链完整，证据充分。\n\n---\n\n**建议动作：**\n\n发独立 security issue，不在公开 issue 区讨论。\n\n**草稿已备好（直接可用）：**\n\n**Title:** [Security]: /pair approve bypasses admin scope guard via plugin command path\n\n**正文核心：**\n- 第1段：问题描述 + 组件路径\n- 第2段：根因（line 471 guard 依赖 `options?.callerScopes`，plugin 命令没传）\n- 第3段：影响（pairing-scoped operator 可通过 chat 命令升级为 admin token）\n- 第4段：复现步骤（与 RPC 路径对比）\n- 第5段：修复方向（thread `ctx.gatewayClientScopes` 进 handler，补测试）\n- 第6段：按 security advisory 处理\n\n草稿全文已在上条消息发出（sessions_send 超时但消息已发起）。如需我补发或调整内容，直接告。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774673045274},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent-to-agent announce step."}],"timestamp":1774673164078,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3","sourceChannel":"feishu","sourceTool":"sessions_send"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Main has sent an agent-to-agent announce step. This is just a heartbeat/system message. I should reply NO_REPLY."},{"type":"text","text":"NO_REPLY"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774673164082}],"truncated":false,"droppedMessages":false,"contentTruncated":false,"contentRedacted":false,"bytes":9146},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774673505648}}
