{"type":"message","id":"1120eca0","parentId":"5acd2c97","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:52:02.255Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, `gh` is authenticated. Now let me create the security advisory. I'll use `gh api` to create it via GraphQL. Let me first try using the `gh advisories` command.\n\nActually, looking at the GitHub CLI docs, `gh advisories create` is available. Let me check what fields are needed.\n\nThe command format would be:\n```\ngh advisories create \\\n  --repo openclaw/openclaw \\\n  --title \"...\" \\\n  --description \"...\" \\\n  --severity critical \\\n  --cvss-score 9.9 \\\n  --ghsa-id ... \\\n  --submit\n```\n\nBut actually, security advisories on GitHub are submitted via the web UI typically. Let me try `gh advisories create` to see if it works.\n\n\nI'll attempt to create this via the GraphQL API instead. I'm constructing a mutation to create a security advisory, but I realize I don't have the complete details like the vulnerable package name or version range needed for the query. I should first check what parameters are actually required for this command.","thinkingSignature":"f9041e7cc738edc607f4ad6b3088ce403c91fc246458336245164e58fae3affb"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ixym63r0arqc_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh advisories create --help 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":38968,"output":253,"cacheRead":22915,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":62136,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774673513946}}
