uest that requests operator.admin scopes via /pair approve. This escalates the operator to full admin capability on the target node, bypassing the RPC authorization check.\\n\\n### Reproduction\\n1. Enable device-pair plugin with operator that has operator.write + operator.pairing but NOT operator.admin\\n2. Create pending device-pairing request requesting role: operator and scopes: [operator.admin]\\n3. From operator chat session, send /pair approve latest\\n4. Pairing is approved; device receives admin token\\n5. Same approval via device.pair.approve RPC is correctly rejected with missing scope: operator.admin\\n\\n### Suggested Fix\\nThread ctx.gatewayClientScopes as callerScopes through the /pair approve handler into approveDevicePairing(), and add a test replicating the RPC authorization test.\\n\\n### Disclosure\\nThis is a real security bypass. Please treat as a security advisory. Happy to follow responsible disclosure process if preferred.\",\n      \"severity\": \"CRITICAL\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":43197,"output":599,"cacheRead":22915,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66711,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774673596845}}
