{"type":"message","id":"9226917c","parentId":"5cae8460","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:53:37.724Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The GraphQL API doesn't seem to support `createSecurityAdvisory` mutation directly on the public API. This is because GitHub's security advisories are managed through their specialized infrastructure. \n\nLet me try using `gh api` with the `--method` flag for the REST API, or check if there's another approach.\n\nActually, looking at GitHub's API documentation more carefully - security advisories (Private Vulnerability Reporting) might need to be submitted through a different mechanism. The PVR (Private Vulnerability Reporting) feature allows security researchers to report vulnerabilities privately, but the `createSecurityAdvisory` mutation might only be available to GitHub's internal systems or require special permissions.\n \nI think the simpler path here is to just open the web browser and submit the advisory directly through GitHub's interface.","thinkingSignature":"3ece69898c69576b7ef6da837438879ed7d9a75412ffade4e3df7bec2c12cffe"},{"type":"text","text":"GraphQL API 不支持直接创建 security advisory（这是 GitHub 内部管理接口）。PVR 需要通过 Web UI 提交。\n\n让我直接打开浏览器到提交页面：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8ywqianehks0_1","name":"browser","arguments":{"action":"open","profile":"openclaw","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security/advisories/new"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":44119,"output":254,"cacheRead":22915,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67288,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774673610552}}
{"type":"message","id":"5bac1db5","parentId":"9226917c","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:53:37.865Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_8ywqianehks0_1","toolName":"browser","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"error\",\n  \"tool\": \"browser\",\n  \"error\": \"Error: No supported browser found (Chrome/Brave/Edge/Chromium on macOS, Linux, or Windows).\"\n}"}],"details":{"status":"error","tool":"browser","error":"Error: No supported browser found (Chrome/Brave/Edge/Chromium on macOS, Linux, or Windows)."},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774673617844}}
{"type":"message","id":"28dec860","parentId":"5bac1db5","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:53:49.869Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No browser available. Let me provide the user with a direct link and the pre-filled content so they can submit it themselves. I'll give them all the details they need.","thinkingSignature":"10e9550e88c7a411428e1c26c29f8befe8c27727323a600bb999c005afd88e10"},{"type":"text","text":"没浏览器环境。给你准备好所有内容，你直接点链接填进去：\n\n🔗 **提交地址：** https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security/advisories/new\n\n---\n\n**预填内容：**\n\n| 字段 | 值 |\n|---|---|\n| **Title** | `[Security] /pair approve bypasses admin scope guard via plugin command path` |\n| **Severity** | Critical |\n| **CVSS Score** | 9.9 |\n\n**Description（直接复制粘贴）：**\n\n```\n## Security Vulnerability — Auth Bypass in device-pair Plugin\n\n### Component\nextensions/device-pair/index.ts — /pair approve command handler\n\n### Description\nThe /pair approve slash command in the device-pair plugin bypasses the admin-scope authorization guard that is correctly enforced on the RPC device-pair approval path.\n\n### Root Cause\napproveDevicePairing() in src/infra/device-pairing.ts guards admin-scope approvals behind an options?.callerScopes check (line 471). When callerScopes is not provided, the guard is skipped entirely.\n\nThe RPC handler in src/gateway/server-methods/devices.ts correctly passes callerScopes, validated by server.device-pair-approve-authz.test.ts:92 — pairing-scoped callers are rejected when approving admin-scope requests.\n\nHowever, the plugin command handler calls approveDevicePairing(pending.requestId) without forwarding ctx.gatewayClientScopes, so callerScopes is undefined and the guard never fires.\n\n### Impact\nAn operator session with only operator.pairing scope (but without operator.admin) can approve a pending device-pairing request that requests operator.admin scopes via /pair approve. This escalates the operator to full admin capability on the target node, bypassing the RPC authorization check.\n\n### Reproduction\n1. Enable device-pair plugin with operator that has operator.write + operator.pairing but NOT operator.admin\n2. Create pending device-pairing request requesting role: operator and scopes: [operator.admin]\n3. From operator chat session, send /pair approve latest\n4. Pairing is approved; device receives admin token\n5. Same approval via device.pair.approve RPC is correctly rejected with missing scope: operator.admin\n\n### Suggested Fix\nThread ctx.gatewayClientScopes as callerScopes through the /pair approve handler into approveDevicePairing(), and add a test replicating the RPC authorization test.\n\n### Disclosure\nThis is a real security bypass. Please treat as a security advisory. Happy to follow responsible disclosure process if preferred.\n```\n\n---\n\n你自己在浏览器打开那个链接，填进去提交就行。提交完告诉我，我好记录到项目文件里。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":44432,"output":561,"cacheRead":22915,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67908,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774673617864}}
{"type":"message","id":"70903ca1","parentId":"28dec860","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:58:29.639Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b5341b1f29d34b25d95dea100130\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n  \"sender\": \"范\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-03-28 12:58 GMT+8\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true,\n  \"was_mentioned\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"范 (ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"name\": \"范\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b5341b1f29d34b25d95dea100130]\n范: geihub页面中还有这几项 教我怎么填\n\n\nAffected products\nEcosystem：\nPackage name：\nAffected versions：\nPatched versions：\n\nSeverity：Critical\nVector string：\n\nWeaknesses\nCommon weakness enumerator (CWE)\n\n[System: The content may include mention tags in the form <at user_id=\"...\">name</at>. Treat these as real mentions of Feishu entities (users or bots).]\n[System: If user_id is \"ou_9422b67a82e7df485a188469c448adb7\", that mention refers to you.]"}],"timestamp":1774673909607}}
{"type":"message","id":"8d0e851d","parentId":"70903ca1","timestamp":"2026-03-28T04:58:53.510Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking how to fill in the remaining fields in the GitHub security advisory form. Let me provide the specific values for:\n\n1. **Affected products / Ecosystem** - This is about the npm/ecosystem package. OpenClaw is a Node.js project, so the ecosystem is likely \"npm\"\n2. **Package name** - `openclaw`\n3. **Affected versions** - Need to check what versions are affected. The issue was reported now, so likely all versions before the fix are affected\n4. **Patched versions** - Not yet patched (no fix released yet)\n5. **Severity** - Critical (already selected)\n6. **Vector string** - CVSS vector string for 9.9 score\n\n\n7. **CWE** - Looking at the vulnerability type, this is an authorization bypass where the plugin command path lacks proper scope validation compared to the RPC path\n\nFor the CVSS vector, a 9.9 critical score with that breakdown suggests a network-exploitable vulnerability with high confidentiality and integrity impact but no authentication requirement.","thinkingSignature":"434b9a43a09e2d207f0a101ff05c43b51d0af4cc6d782a5efbfbab71c777dccd"},{"type":"text","text":"直接告诉你怎么填：\n\n| 字段 | 值 |\n|---|---|\n| **Ecosystem** | `npm` |\n| **Package name** | `openclaw` |\n| **Affected versions** | `>=0.0.0`（所有版本均受影响，暂无补丁） |\n| **Patched versions** | `暂无`（留空，或填 `none` / `N/A`） |\n| **Severity** | ✅ Critical（已选） |\n| **Vector string** | `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N` |\n| **CWE** | `CWE-862`（Missing Authorization，授权检查缺失） |\n\n---\n\n**说明：**\n\n- **Ecosystem** 选 `npm`，因为 openclaw 是 npm 包\n- **Affected versions** 填 `>=0.0.0` 表示所有版本都有这个问题，直到补丁发布\n- **Patched versions** 留空或填 `none`，因为目前还没有修复版本\n- **CVSS Vector**：`AV:N`（网络可利用）+ `AC:L`（低复杂度）+ `PR:L`（低权限即可利用）+ `S:C`（影响范围 Changed）+ `C:H/I:H/A:N`（高机密性/完整性，无可用性影响）→ 综合得分 9.9\n- **CWE-862**：授权检查缺失（Authorization Missing），最符合这个漏洞根因\n\n填完直接 Submit 就行。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79,"output":542,"cacheRead":22915,"cacheWrite":43789,"totalTokens":67325,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774673909624}}
