{"type":"message","id":"3aaf748d","parentId":"67120cad","timestamp":"2026-03-28T05:13:37.762Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We have Node.js and npm but no Chrome/Chromium browser. The agent-browser skill uses a headless browser backend. Without a browser binary, we can't actually use this skill.\n\nHowever, even without a browser, we could potentially use puppeteer or playwright which bundle their own browsers. Let me check if there are any browser binaries available or if we can install one.\n\nActually, the better question is: is it worth installing a browser for this kind of automation? The main use cases would be:\n1. Filling the GitHub security advisory form (done now)\n2. Automating GitHub issue/PR interactions\n3. Running browser-based tests\n\nFor the GitHub security advisory, we already got through it manually. For GitHub operations, we can use the `gh` CLI for most things. The main gap was just the web form submission.\n\nLet me think about whether it's worth the effort:\n- Installing a full browser (Chromium is several hundred MBs)\n- The agent-browser skill setup\n- ongoing maintenance\n\nFor the value: it would help with:\n\n\n- GitHub web forms (security advisories, some settings)\n- Web scraping/data extraction\n- UI testing\n\nBut we can already do most GitHub operations via `gh` CLI. The browser is mainly useful for web forms that don't have API equivalents. Given the resource cost and that we've already manually submitted the security advisory, I'm leaning toward recommending we skip this unless there's a specific, recurring task that absolutely requires browser automation.","thinkingSignature":"19f74e6638aa7be547da54df50957a67f932ff82a9856c630a59bf8fec063bac"},{"type":"text","text":"有个矛盾：\n\n**装了就能用吗？** 未必。我们有 Node.js，但没 Chrome/Chromium 二进制。`agent-browser` 底层需要浏览器引擎，Linux 上通常要装 Chromium（几百MB），加上依赖环境。\n\n**装了能解决什么？**\n- ✅ GitHub web 表单自动化（刚才 PVR 表格就是例子）\n- ✅ 网页数据抓取\n- ✅ UI 测试\n\n**但我们其实已经能搞定大部分：**\n- `gh` CLI → 覆盖 80% 的 GitHub 操作（issues、PRs、advisories 等）\n- GitHub 有完整 REST API → 剩余 20% 也能绕过去\n\n**我的判断：优先级不高。** 原因：\n1. 这次 PVR 表单虽然没浏览器，但我们有完整预填内容，填进去也就 2 分钟\n2. 真正需要浏览器的场景极少（GitHub 设置页面的 form submit 这种）\n3. 装浏览器+环境配置本身有维护成本\n\n**如果你觉得浏览器自动化很有价值**（比如经常要操作没有 API 的第三方 web 界面），我可以装。但目前这个项目里，GitHub 操作基本用 `gh` CLI 够用了。\n\n先不装，你觉得有必要的时候再说？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":51253,"output":564,"cacheRead":22915,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":74732,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774674798727}}
{"type":"message","id":"098fc17a","parentId":"3aaf748d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T05:13:38.630Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b53427f28893cb224335ace7abe3\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n  \"sender\": \"范\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-03-28 13:13 GMT+8\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true,\n  \"was_mentioned\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"范 (ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"name\": \"范\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b53427f28893cb224335ace7abe3]\n范: 对了，今天提交的 P44 ，我们的OpenClaw版本是 2026.3.8，不是最新版本，是否应该更新到最新版本，再重新测试一遍\n\n[System: The content may include mention tags in the form <at user_id=\"...\">name</at>. Treat these as real mentions of Feishu entities (users or bots).]\n[System: If user_id is \"ou_9422b67a82e7df485a188469c448adb7\", that mention refers to you.]"}],"timestamp":1774674818623}}
{"type":"message","id":"af224435","parentId":"098fc17a","timestamp":"2026-03-28T05:13:56.035Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user makes a very good point. The vulnerability #55994 was reported on GitHub and we've been analyzing it. But the question is about our own OpenClaw version - we're running 2026.3.8, not the latest (which appears to be 2026.3.24 based on earlier cron scan results). \n\nThe question is: should we upgrade to the latest version and re-verify the vulnerability?\n\nKey considerations:\n1. The vulnerability is in the device-pair plugin code path, not version-specific - the bug is in the code logic (missing `callerScopes` parameter forwarding), which exists in all versions\n\n\n2. Upgrading is straightforward: `npm install -g openclaw@latest` followed by a gateway restart\n3. Before upgrading though, I should verify whether the vulnerability is actually present in our current version by examining our device-pairing.ts file, and then upgrade and retest to see if the issue persists\n\nSince this is a code-level auth bypass rather than a version-specific bug, it's likely present across all versions until a patch is released - but running through the actual exploitation steps in our environment would definitively confirm whether it's exploitable here.","thinkingSignature":"3001d7a021a7792490d1738e8c5f49a54451a570ce6ee5c27515a1353dd00334"},{"type":"text","text":"好问题。但这个漏洞情况特殊：\n\n**漏洞本身是代码级 bug，不是版本问题。** 根因是 `approveDevicePairing()` 少传了一个参数，所有版本只要代码里没修就有问题。跟咱们用 2026.3.8 还是 3.24 无关——除非 maintainer 已经悄悄修了某个版本。\n\n**不过你说得对，应该验证一下：**\n1. 先查我们现在的代码里，那个 guard 是不是真的没传 `callerScopes`\n2. 再升级到最新版，看 maintainer 有没有已经修过\n\n让我先查一下我们现有版本：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_yagyg7htlf0c_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw --version 2>/dev/null || cat /root/.openclaw/workspace/openclaw/package.json | grep '\"version\"' | head -1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","