{"type":"message","id":"0731e4a1","parentId":"edddc4b9","timestamp":"2026-03-28T05:29:05.267Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the information I need. Let me:\n\n1. Confirm P44 vulnerability is still in 2026.3.24 (confirmed - the code at line 471 still has the same guard)\n2. The weixin issue #55994 - the user is on 2026.3.13, and the error message is \"Poll fields require action 'poll'\" which is the same guard that was added for Telegram. But the guard is at the `runMessageAction` level, not channel-specific. So the issue is that wechat is somehow triggering poll parameter detection.\n3. Now I need to check the other issues/PRs we submitted.\n\nLet me also check the status of our other PRs and issues.\n\n\nI should verify whether our other open pull requests and issues are still pending review or have been updated by the maintainers.","thinkingSignature":"88114c0856271d5f7f6e45c20dd6fb07580e2bb543ab6cf317e7bdbcf45a07c4"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_yd1te6z379e1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue view 54952 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json body,comments,labels --jq '{state: .state, labels: [.labels[].name], comments: .total_count}' 2>&1\ngh issue view 54964 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json body,comments,labels --jq '{state: .state, labels: [.labels[].name], comments: .total_count}' 2>&1\ngh pr view 55008 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json state,reviews,comments --jq '{state: .state, reviews: [.reviews[] | {author: .author.login, state: .state}], comments: .total_count}' 2>&1\ngh pr view 55013 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json state,reviews,comments --jq '{state: .state, reviews: [.reviews[] | {author: .author.login, state: .state}], comments: .total_count}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":57156,"output":400,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":80181,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"sto