{"type":"message","id":"03420ca1","parentId":"bfc6ab69","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:33:18.732Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me also look at whether there are any new Feishu issues that haven't been addressed yet. Let me also look at a few more PRs that are relevant to our setup.Let me also scan for issues related to our specific use case - multi-agent setups, Feishu routing, etc.Actually, let me also think about what we could contribute directly. We have identified several gaps in the project. Let me think about what would be a good NEW issue or PR we could author that would be high value for the community.One idea: the Feishu routing fallback behavior - we've confirmed the diagnostics gap but haven't really dug into documenting what the actual fallback chain looks like in detail. \n\nI'm thinking about drafting a more technical issue on the Feishu routing fallback chain, or maybe proposing improvements around cron session state management. But I should be strategic with my time—let me focus on the most actionable items: reviewing #56240 since it's about plugin registry for sub-agents (which matters for our multi-agent setup) and checking whether #56158 is a duplicate of #56244 before moving forward.","thinkingSignature":"247fd65ebcb4eaa7a784d73e9a9a8fe6189f94026075c9bc9b2f94eb66dbb328"},{"type":"text","text":"顺手再支持 #56167（NO_REPLY 泄露问题，直接影响我们的 Feishu 使用）。\n\n现在看看有没有值得主动去挖的新方向。xixi 之前扫的时候发现了 #56127（WhatsApp 插件未配置也加载导致崩溃）是个高优先级 regression，让我深入看一下。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2ruukce42y1m_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue view 56127 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json number,title,state,comments,labels,body --jq '{number,title,state,comment_count:(.comments|length),labels:[.labels[].name],body}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":45310,"output":362,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":68297,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683186957,"responseId":"0616b73330b9fff63f80c20a26958c99"}}
{"type":"message","id":"04d4c98d","parentId":"03420ca1","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:33:19.229Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_2ruukce42y1m_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nWhatsApp plugin crashes the agent on every message with \\\"missing light-runtime-api\\\" error even when WhatsApp was never configured or installed. Affects both the OpenClaw dashboard chat and Telegram channel. Issue persists on 2026.3.24.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Install OpenClaw inside a Hostinger Docker container via npm: `npm install -g openclaw@latest`\\n2. Start gateway: `openclaw gateway`\\n3. Configure Telegram channel only — do not configure or install WhatsApp\\n4. Send any message via the OpenClaw dashboard chat or Telegram\\n5. Observe agent crash with WhatsApp runtime error\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nAgent responds to messages normally via the dashboard chat and Telegram. WhatsApp plugin should not load or interfere when it has never been configured.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\n```\\nError: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\nEmbedded agent failed before reply: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\n```\\n\\nThe WhatsApp plugin appears to load automatically at gateway startup even when never configured, crashing the agent on every incoming message.\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24 (Hostinger Docker container)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\nnpm global (`npm install -g openclaw@latest`) inside Docker container\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nanthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nopenclaw (gateway) → anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\nAnthropic API key configured via `openclaw configure`. Standard `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` setup. Gateway mode set to local.\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```\\n[diagnostic] lane task error: lane=session:agent:main:main error=\\\"Error: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\\"\\nEmbedded agent failed before reply: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\n[health-monitor] [whatsapp:default] health-monitor: restarting (reason: stopped)\\n[health-monitor] [whatsapp:default] health-monitor: restart failed: Error: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n**Affected:** Users running OpenClaw 2026.3.24 in Docker environments who have never configured WhatsApp\\n**Severity:** High — blocks all agent responses via dashboard chat; Telegram workaround available but requires full channel reconfiguration\\n**Frequency:** Always — 100% reproducible\\n\\nThe following workarounds were attempted without success:\\n- `openclaw plugins uninstall whatsapp` — error: *\\\"Plugin 'whatsapp' is not managed by plugins config/install records and cannot be uninstalled\\\"*\\n- Disabling via `openclaw.json` using `plugins.whatsapp.enabled: false` — config validation error: *\\\"Unrecognized key: whatsapp\\\"*\\n- `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` — same config validation error\\n- `openclaw doctor --fix` — did not resolve the issue\\n\\nA config-level opt-out such as `channels.whatsapp.enabled: false` would be a helpful workaround until the runtime files are properly bundled.\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\nTelegram is functional after full channel reconfiguration. The dashboard chat remains broken. The WhatsApp plugin appears to register itself as a built-in channel at gateway startup with no supported mechanism to disable or remove it.\",\"comment_count\":0,\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56127,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[Bug]: Agent failed before reply: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'.\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":452,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nWhatsApp plugin crashes the agent on every message with \\\"missing light-runtime-api\\\" error even when WhatsApp was never configured or installed. Affects both the OpenClaw dashboard chat and Telegram channel. Issue persists on 2026.3.24.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Install OpenClaw inside a Hostinger Docker container via npm: `npm install -g openclaw@latest`\\n2. Start gateway: `openclaw gateway`\\n3. Configure Telegram channel only — do not configure or install WhatsApp\\n4. Send any message via the OpenClaw dashboard chat or Telegram\\n5. Observe agent crash with WhatsApp runtime error\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nAgent responds to messages normally via the dashboard chat and Telegram. WhatsApp plugin should not load or interfere when it has never been configured.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\n```\\nError: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\nEmbedded agent failed before reply: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\n```\\n\\nThe WhatsApp plugin appears to load automatically at gateway startup even when never configured, crashing the agent on every incoming message.\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24 (Hostinger Docker container)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\nnpm global (`npm install -g openclaw@latest`) inside Docker container\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nanthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nopenclaw (gateway) → anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\nAnthropic API key configured via `openclaw configure`. Standard `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` setup. Gateway mode set to local.\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```\\n[diagnostic] lane task error: lane=session:agent:main:main error=\\\"Error: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\\"\\nEmbedded agent failed before reply: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\n[health-monitor] [whatsapp:default] health-monitor: restarting (reason: stopped)\\n[health-monitor] [whatsapp:default] health-monitor: restart failed: Error: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n**Affected:** Users running OpenClaw 2026.3.24 in Docker environments who have never configured WhatsApp\\n**Severity:** High — blocks all agent responses via dashboard chat; Telegram workaround available but requires full channel reconfiguration\\n**Frequency:** Always — 100% reproducible\\n\\nThe following workarounds were attempted without success:\\n- `openclaw plugins uninstall whatsapp` — error: *\\\"Plugin 'whatsapp' is not managed by plugins config/install records and cannot be uninstalled\\\"*\\n- Disabling via `openclaw.json` using `plugins.whatsapp.enabled: false` — config validation error: *\\\"Unrecognized key: whatsapp\\\"*\\n- `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/whatsapp` — same config validation error\\n- `openclaw doctor --fix` — did not resolve the issue\\n\\nA config-level opt-out such as `channels.whatsapp.enabled: false` would be a helpful workaround until the runtime files are properly bundled.\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\nTelegram is functional after full channel reconfiguration. The dashboard chat remains broken. The WhatsApp plugin appears to register itself as a built-in channel at gateway startup with no supported mechanism to disable or remove it.\",\"comment_count\":0,\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56127,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[Bug]: Agent failed before reply: WhatsApp plugin runtime is unavailable: missing light-runtime-api for plugin 'whatsapp'.\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774683199205}}
{"type":"message","id":"62de64f0","parentId":"04d4c98d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:33:26.681Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"#56127 is a critical regression - the WhatsApp plugin loads automatically even when not configured, and crashes the agent on every message. The issue is very well documented with clear reproduction steps and impact analysis.\n\nHowever, there's no PR fixing this yet. Let me check if there's a PR that addresses this.\n\nThis is a bug where the WhatsApp plugin bundles a `light-runtime-api` that's missing. This is a bundling/distribution issue rather than a code logic issue. The workaround is also blocked because you can't disable the WhatsApp plugin via config.\n\nThis is a good candidate for us to:\n1. Support the issue with a comment confirming it's affecting us\n\n\n2. Maybe propose a workaround or root cause analysis\n\nNow I'm scanning through the open PRs to see if any of them address this specific issue.","thinkingSignature":"96087e003f0479dbab8a4ef5c487084c195a61c01b9df9b9effe04a9778c52f3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5xldydjym8dh_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr list --repo openclaw/openclaw --state open --limit 30 --search \"whatsapp\" --json number,title,author,labels --jq '.[] | {number,.title,.author:.author.login,labels:[.labels[].name]}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":46562,"output":243,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":69430,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683199230,"responseId":"0616b73f8a3d8163886576788c5f242c"}}
{"type":"message","id":"e521844d","parentId":"62de64f0","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:33:27.493Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_5xldydjym8dh_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"failed to parse jq expression (line 1, column 15)\n    .[] | {number,.title,.author:.author.login,labels:[.labels[].name]}\n                  ^  unexpected token \".title\"\n\n(Command exited with code 1)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":1,"durationMs":729,"aggregated":"failed to parse jq expression (line 1, column 15)\n    .[] | {number,.title,.author:.author.login,labels:[.labels[].name]}\n                  ^  unexpected token \".title\"\n\n(Command exited with code 1)","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774683207475}}
