{"type":"message","id":"45c92348","parentId":"fcaafde8","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:38:30.680Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me continue with other proactive work. I should also check if there are any new issues or PRs that I haven't supported yet. Let me do a quick scan of recent open issues and PRs.Actually, let me now think about what we could do next:1. We could look for more small PRs to support\n2. We could draft a new issue if we find a gap\n3. We could look at the cron feedback to see if any of our previous comments got responses\n4. We could look at what xixi is working on\n\nSince I don't want to just keep scanning PRs endlessly, let me focus on something more targeted. Let me look at whether there are any docs PRs (size XS/S) that address documentation gaps we've noticed in our own usage of OpenClaw.One thing I've noticed: the Feishu routing docs are spread across multiple files and not entirely clear. \n\nIf I have time, I could draft a documentation PR to consolidate and clarify those Feishu routing docs, but first let me check if there are any cron feedback responses I should follow up on.","thinkingSignature":"317dd157b26e62a46c0f478b9077798c639cccea24c5560406fc5d861aa58ee7"},{"type":"text","text":"好。现在去检查一下 cron 反馈记录——看看有没有 maintainer 回复我们的 PR/issue。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_q2tidh1aefx1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/openclaw-feedback-check.txt 2>/dev/null || echo \"File not found\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":58618,"output":299,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":81542,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683501201,"responseId":"0616b86d25589b7cd4fbd7d28a12c96a"}}
