S\"],\"number\":56209,\"title\":\"fix(plugins): clear matrix-js-sdk entrypoint flag before jiti plugin loads\"}\n{\"author\":\"w-sss\",\"created\":\"2026-03-28\",\"labels\":[\"agents\",\"size: XS\"],\"number\":56204,\"title\":\"fix: restore getApiKey callback after streamFn override (#55816)\"}\n{\"author\":\"RevisitMoon\",\"created\":\"2026-03-28\",\"labels\":[\"agents\",\"size: S\"],\"number\":56203,\"title\":\"fix(sessions_send): prefer sessionKey over label when both are present (AI-assisted)\"}\n{\"author\":\"moortekweb-art\",\"created\":\"2026-03-28\",\"labels\":[\"channel: signal\",\"gateway\",\"size: S\"],\"number\":56202,\"title\":\"fix: generate systemd gateway env files\"}\n{\"author\":\"Talegqz\",\"created\":\"2026-03-28\",\"labels\":[\"size: S\"],\"number\":56196,\"title\":\"fix(skills): load skill commands regardless of model alias configuration\"}\n{\"author\":\"chrysb\",\"created\":\"2026-03-28\",\"labels\":[\"gateway\",\"size: XS\"],\"number\":56195,\"title\":\"fix(gateway): preserve operator scopes for shared-auth connections\"}\n{\"author\":\"evanjacobson\",\"created\":\"2026-03-28\",\"labels\":[\"size: S\"],\"number\":56190,\"title\":\"config: support ${VAR:-default} env var fallbacks\"}\n{\"author\":\"bugkill3r\",\"created\":\"2026-03-28\",\"labels\":[\"size: XS\"],\"number\":56189,\"title\":\"fix: include BOOTSTRAP.md template in npm package (#56155)\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774683582030}}
{"type":"message","id":"d116296d","parentId":"eadbb103","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:39:50.243Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at this list of recent PRs I haven't supported yet, let me pick out the ones that are most relevant to our setup:1. **#56258** - per-subsystem timeouts on shutdown close handler. This could be relevant to our timeout issues.2. **#56257** - declarative capabilities model in plugin manifest. Interesting for plugin authors.3. **#56256** - skill integrity verification with SHA-256 hashing. Security feature.4. **#56242** - CJK error patterns for failover classification. This could be relevant if we use models that output CJK characters.5. \n\nI'm seeing several others that might matter less for us right now—systemd env files, agent:turn:end hooks, matrix-js-sdk flags, and env var fallbacks are either tangential or already covered. Though that shutdown timeout issue #56258 seems worth looking into more closely since it's specifically about graceful shutdown handling.","thinkingSignature":"19986e12dfdf9e5f71cc18247c6156f8a3307ac80ffe8001a3681bb49f730fe9"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_xcwk8m8omvx9_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56258 --jq '.body[0:400]'\necho \"===\"\ngh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56242 --jq '.body[0:300]'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":62839,"output":262,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":85726,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683582058,"responseId":"0616b8bed9141b29cf05aea39ac6fba6"}}
{"type":"message","id":"7dfe8abd","parentId":"d116296d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:39:51.946Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_xcwk8m8omvx9_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\n- A single hung subsystem `stop()` call (e.g. Telegram polling stuck during network recovery) can consume the entire 25 s `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS` budget, preventing remaining subsystems from cleaning up and forcing users to `kill -9` the gateway process.\n- Wrap each async stop/close call in `createGatewayCloseHandler` with a 5 s per-subsystem `raceTimeout`. When a subsystem exceeds its b\n===\n## Problem\n\nChinese LLM providers (ZhipuAI/GLM, Bailian/Alibaba Cloud, Kimi/Moonshot, DeepSeek, etc.) return error messages in Chinese. The existing failover classification only matches English patterns, causing these errors to fall through as unclassified — surfacing raw provider errors to users in"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1665,"aggregated":"## Summary\n\n- A single hung subsystem `stop()` call (e.g. Telegram polling stuck during network recovery) can consume the entire 25 s `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS` budget, preventing remaining subsystems from cleaning up and forcing users to `kill -9` the gateway process.\n- Wrap each async stop/close call in `createGatewayCloseHandler` with a 5 s per-subsystem `raceTimeout`. When a subsystem exceeds its b\n===\n## Problem\n\nChinese LLM providers (ZhipuAI/GLM, Bailian/Alibaba Cloud, Kimi/Moonshot, DeepSeek, etc.) return error messages in Chinese. The existing failover classification only matches English patterns, causing these errors to fall through as unclassified — surfacing raw provider errors to users in","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774683591926}}
{"type":"message","id":"742bf61a","parentId":"7dfe8abd","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:39:58.072Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"#56258 is about per-subsystem timeouts on shutdown. This is a good reliability fix - a single hung subsystem can consume the entire shutdown budget. Let me support this PR.\n\n#56242 is about CJK error patterns for failover classification - Chinese LLM providers return errors in Chinese, but the failover classification only matches English patterns. This is relevant if we're using Chinese LLM providers. Let me support this too.","thinkingSignature":"d0542c8db9dcf2bcdcb23d921b3b24f3f653ea954970464611e58bfe54837d3e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_hdrkg2kqjkvs_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr comment 56258 --repo openclaw/openclaw --body \"This addresses a real gateway reliability issue — a single hung subsystem stop() call (e.g. Telegram polling during network recovery) can consume the entire SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS budget, forcing users to kill -9. The per-subsystem raceTimeout approach is the right pattern. S-sized fix with meaningful reliability improvement. LGTM, requesting maintainer review.\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":63275,"output":196,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86096,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683591948,"responseId":"0616b8c82018f56a96659f6cc580ea8f"}}
