{"type":"message","id":"204f7664","parentId":"0fecdeaf","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:40:53.740Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! Let me check the PRs with more than 1 comment to see if there are new responses:- #56247: 5 comments (more than before - we've supported it, so our comment was added)\n- #56244: 2 comments (we added one)\n- #56204: 2 comments (we added one)\n- #56250: 2 comments (we added one)\n- #56212: 6 comments (we added one - there were already 5 before us!)- #56223: 2 comments (we added one)- #56243: 2 comments (we added one)\n\n\n- #56258: 2 comments (we added one)\n- #56242: 2 comments (we added one)\n\nNow I need to verify which PRs had existing comments before our support, since that's crucial for understanding their current state.","thinkingSignature":"1f3e60bd93bfbe9e62d1435777d52ddbc1591b458bdbea5fcf2308438e583e9b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0fwv38qq00a4_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56212/comments --jq '.[] | {author:.author.login,body:.body[0:200]}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":64991,"output":237,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":87853,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683646139,"responseId":"0616b8fe91f6b465d3359e4efa579ce8"}}
{"type":"message","id":"7d2e5dd0","parentId":"204f7664","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:40:54.275Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_0fwv38qq00a4_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve announce fallback when delivery target is set**\\n\\nDefaulting `resolvedMode` to `\\\"none\\\"` for every `hasDe\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"This looks like it flips an existing/defaulted contract rather than fixing just the no-target case. `resolveCronDeliveryPlan()` currently treats a present `delivery` object with no `mode` as `announce\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"thank you！\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve accountId key when clearing announce delivery**\\n\\nWhen editing an announce job that already has `deliver\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve webhook bestEffort in cron delivery payload**\\n\\nThe webhook branch drops `bestEffort`, so jobs created/e\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Keep skills status commands on the same workspace context**\\n\\nThis change makes install/update resolve workspace \"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":489,"aggregated":"{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve announce fallback when delivery target is set**\\n\\nDefaulting `resolvedMode` to `\\\"none\\\"` for every `hasDe\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"This looks like it flips an existing/defaulted contract rather than fixing just the no-target case. `resolveCronDeliveryPlan()` currently treats a present `delivery` object with no `mode` as `announce\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"thank you！\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve accountId key when clearing announce delivery**\\n\\nWhen editing an announce job that already has `deliver\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve webhook bestEffort in cron delivery payload**\\n\\nThe webhook branch drops `bestEffort`, so jobs created/e\"}\n{\"author\":null,\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Keep skills status commands on the same workspace context**\\n\\nThis change makes install/update resolve workspace \"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774683654251}}
{"type":"message","id":"bc2688cc","parentId":"7d2e5dd0","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:41:02.380Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The comments on #56212 are not from our comment - there are 6 pre-existing comments from what looks like an automated system or a detailed reviewer. These are substantive comments with P1/P2 badges suggesting this PR has some review issues.\n\nThe comments show:\n1. \"Preserve announce fallback when delivery target is set\" - suggesting the fix might break existing behavior\n2. \"This looks like it flips an existing/defaulted contract rather than fixing just the no-target case\" - this is a valid concern\n3. \"thank you！\" - author response\n4-6. More P1/P2 badge comments\n\nThis is concerning - #56212 might have review issues that we accidentally supported without knowing. Let me check what the actual state is.","thinkingSignature":"7c1c6807a00b1ce64f7fd9d40c84a2db708b1a8b058fc32199b048584176a51c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_h74soc8vfd69_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56212 --jq '{state,reviewDecision,title}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":65630,"output":201,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88456,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683654278,"responseId":"0616b906c17916556a996805559e1000"}}
{"type":"message","id":"d3215b92","parentId":"bc2688cc","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:41:03.211Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_h74soc8vfd69_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"reviewDecision\":null,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"fix(cron): default to delivery mode 'none' when not explicitly set\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":793,"aggregated":"{\"reviewDecision\":null,\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"fix(cron): default to delivery mode 'none' when not explicitly set\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774683663189}}
{"type":"message","id":"a7c91e6e","parentId":"d3215b92","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:41:14.274Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The #56212 PR has reviewDecision: null which means no formal review has been requested. The comments are from some kind of automated review system or a detailed commenter. The comments suggest there might be issues with the PR's approach - it might be changing an existing contract rather than fixing the specific issue.\n\nSince I already commented on this PR supporting it, I should note this concern. But since the PR is still open and has no formal review decision, it might be that the author has addressed the concerns or the maintainers disagree with the commenter.\n\nActually, looking at the comments more carefully, these seem to be from someone doing a very detailed code review with P1/P2 badges. \n\nThe core issue seems to be that this PR changes behavior for all cron jobs created via Web UI, not just those without explicit delivery config - it would affect jobs where the user did intentionally set `delivery.mode = undefined` and expected announce fallback. This is a legitimate concern, though I'm not well-positioned to judge the tradeoffs here. I already voiced support for it, so at minimum I should add a follow-up noting the reviewer's valid concern about the existing contract change. Let me check the other PRs with multiple comments to see if there are similar issues.","thinkingSignature":"36e51aababa7787191221c403de277b0ec6b635d70c659b4469d1e27b2214c5d"},{"type":"text","text":"#56212 有些深评意见——有人担心这个 PR 改变了已有 contract 而不只是修复无 target 的 case。先继续看其他 PR 动态。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_knck36ntwnnz_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56247/comments --jq '.[] | {author:.author.login,body:.body[0:150]}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":65875,"output":342,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"t