{"type":"message","id":"1aaf24b6","parentId":"613205a5","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:41:41.642Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, the API says 3 comments but when I fetched the comments I got 5 lines. Let me recheck. Actually, looking again, the jq filter `.[] | {author:.author.login,body:.body[0:150]}` returns an object per comment, so 5 objects = 5 comments. But the API says 3. Maybe the filter `.author.login` returned null for some comments (because the comments are from a bot or something).\n\nThe reviewDecision is still null - no formal review requested. But there are substantive Greptile P1/P2 comments that the author needs to address. Our support comment was the 3rd one.\n\nActually, wait - I said 5 comments in my earlier scan. \n\nAh, I see the issue now - I was checking the issue comments endpoint instead of the PR comments endpoint. So when I ran `gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/56247/comments`, that was pulling from the issue, not the PR itself. The actual PR has 3 comments, which matches what the API is reporting.\n\nBut I'm realizing there's something odd here - when I fetched the comments, some of the `author.login` values came back as null, yet I still got 5 comment objects instead of 3. Let me look more carefully at what's actually being returned, because the count doesn't seem to align with what I'd expect from the data structure.\n\nWait, I think I see the issue - the `.author` field might be returning null for certain comments, which is throwing off my count. Rather than getting caught up in the discrepancy, I should focus on what matters: the substantive P1 and P2 comments from Greptile are still sitting there without author responses, which means this PR probably isn't ready to merge yet. I need to be more careful about which PRs I'm actually supporting, especially ones that already have pending automated reviews.\n\nLooking at what I've supported so far today, #56212 and #56247 both have active review comments that haven't been addressed. Since I can't withdraw my comments, I'll just keep this in mind going forward - no need to flag it unless the user asks specifically.","thinkingSignature":"ce9dbde9c6fcf6c95f0a9ebd6fe7e2b0eb4236734c91f339c0fb8eed5b2f6e2d"},{"type":"text","text":"有些不对劲——#56212 和 #56247 都有 Greptile 的 P1/P2 深评意见（还没被 author 处理），我之前没仔细看就支持了。这是个教训：看到有 review 就要先读完再做判断。\n\n不过评论已经发出去了，继续盯着这两个 PR 看 author 是否回应。其余支持的 PR 没有深评意见，可以继续等 maintainer review。\n\n现在快速扫一下我们之前自己发的那几个 PR 有没有 maintainer 人为回复（不是 Greptile/Codex bot）。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dlsu8fn7au0r_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55008/comments --jq '.[] | {author:.author.login,body:.body[0:100],created:.created_at}'\necho \"===\"\ngh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/55013/comments --jq '.[] | {author:.author.login,body:.body[0:100],created:.created_at}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":66795,"output":649,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":90069,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774683680688,"responseId":"0616b9200b027d30bef7555c9c9a2de6"}}
