{"type":"message","id":"a9e7af22","parentId":"70068f6a","timestamp":"2026-03-28T07:42:04.458Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Our PRs #55008 and #55013 only have Greptile/automated comments, no human maintainer comments. The last comments were from 2026-03-26. No new human feedback.\n\nLet me now think about what else to do. I've been very active today. Let me think strategically about what the next high-value action would be:\n\n1. We've supported many PRs\n2. Our own PRs are waiting for maintainer attention\n3. We have several issues in the tracker\n\nOne thing I haven't done yet: look at whether there's a good first-time contributor PR we could mentor/help review. This would build goodwill with the community.\n \nI should probably stop here and let the system settle. Let me update the project status file with today's progress and wrap up with a summary for the user. Actually, wait—before I do that, I want to quickly check one more thing. There's that Feishu routing issue #54952 we submitted that hasn't gotten traction. Let me see if there's something more specific about Feishu group chat routing I could contribute there, or if we should just wait for maintainer feedback.\n\nI'm realizing I should be more strategic about my next moves. Instead of just scanning through more PRs, let me think about what would actually move the needle. The Feishu routing diagnostics gap issue is still unresolved, and while we suggested a docs approach, maybe the real issue is that the routing behavior itself is wrong. Let me dig into the Feishu channel documentation to understand the actual routing chain and see if there's a concrete problem to solve.","thinkingSignature":"0737ca16d0c6968f3dc82e528b59599617cdaec556888b221120bd4fdc78f5a0"},{"type":"text","text":"我们自己的 PR #55008 和 #55013 都只有 Greptile bot 评论，没人维护者回复。今天已经足够主动了——更新一下项目状态，准备收尾今天的行动。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_3kxt7yrmrmdz_1","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/root/.