{"type":"message","id":"f42d498c","parentId":"617ae9b3","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:46:23.055Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ling is running but the exec commands are taking too long (especially the fork which has a 120s timeout). The session timed out in our main because ling took too long. Ling is actually working but just needs more time.\n\nLet me wait for ling to complete. But since it timed out from our main's perspective, I should either:\n1. Wait for ling to finish and report back\n2. Do it myself\n\nActually, the issue is that ling's exec commands take a very long time (fork + clone could take minutes). This is just a timeout in our session with ling - ling itself might still be running. But we can't wait indefinitely.\n\nLet me just do this myself. I'm the main agent, I can fork and make a small PR directly. The 20-minute timeout issue with ling suggests ling's tasks are too complex and keep timing out.\n\n\nI'll handle the fork myself and guide ling to focus on simpler, faster tasks while I tackle the more involved work directly.","thinkingSignature":"bce26bbca49b7603b803ece6ab1e7a9c40555f19de3633d2372bd894263e897c"},{"type":"text","text":"ling 在跑但 exec 命令太重了（fork + clone 要很久）。我来直接干。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_lmtb7o93zw8e_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh auth status 2>&1 | head -5"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":64347,"output":254,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":87226,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774701972970,"responseId":"06170095f15886cd9cdca166643b8c4b"}}
