{"type":"message","id":"7fded64f","parentId":"97886e67","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:47:06.801Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Clone succeeded. Now let me find a small bug to fix. Let me look at some of the issues we've tracked and find one that's simple enough for a first PR.\n\nOptions:\n1. #56241 - fix: Config schema rejects legacy messages.tts.edge - simple schema change\n2. #56158/#56244/#56223 - Feishu tool re-registration guards - simple boolean guard\n3. #56186 - fix(ui): preserve config save error after loadChannels refresh\n\nActually, since the clone is shallow (--depth 1), I don't have the full git history. But I can still make changes to files and push.\n\nLet me look at one of the simpler issues. \n\nThe Feishu hot-reload guard looks like a straightforward boolean flag fix. Let me check what the actual code changes would be for these candidates - I should compare the PRs to understand the pattern and pick whichever seems most straightforward to implement.","thinkingSignature":"72d14ffbc3d847fd409f576f2c6d3ef3ebdb9b0a1d04302209130ac959ff0f3b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_iw62qeztpdtq_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56244 --jq '{files:.changed_files,adds:.additions,dels:.deletions,body:.body[0:500]}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":65675,"output":258,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88558,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702017218,"responseId":"061700c1c8ed8a4da95d0ac11dccb9a8"}}
{"type":"message","id":"68726ffc","parentId":"7fded64f","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:47:07.442Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_iw62qeztpdtq_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"adds\":4,\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nFeishu plugin tools re-register repeatedly on config hot-reload (#56114). Every time the config changes and triggers a gateway reload, `registerFull()` is called again, causing all 7 `registerFeishu*Tools()` functions to execute repeatedly and register duplicate tools.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nIn `extensions/feishu/index.ts`, the `registerFull()` callback has no deduplication protection. The plugin system re-invokes each plugin's `register()` on config hot-reload, and `registerFull` blindly r\",\"dels\":0,\"files\":1}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":606,"aggregated":"{\"adds\":4,\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nFeishu plugin tools re-register repeatedly on config hot-reload (#56114). Every time the config changes and triggers a gateway reload, `registerFull()` is called again, causing all 7 `registerFeishu*Tools()` functions to execute repeatedly and register duplicate tools.\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\nIn `extensions/feishu/index.ts`, the `registerFull()` callback has no deduplication protection. The plugin system re-invokes each plugin's `register()` on config hot-reload, and `registerFull` blindly r\",\"dels\":0,\"files\":1}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774702027421}}
{"type":"message","id":"89604c72","parentId":"68726ffc","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:47:20.125Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"#56244 is very small - just 1 file, 4 lines added, 0 deleted. This is a perfect first PR! The fix is a simple boolean guard in `extensions/feishu/index.ts`.\n\nBut wait - #56244 is already submitted by pgsev77. We can't submit the same fix again. Let me check if there's still a meaningful contribution I can make to this issue or if I should pick a different one.\n\nLet me look at #56223 (another duplicate of #56114) - that's by pgsev77 as well. And #56158 is by Talegqz. All three PRs for the same issue already exist. So this is already covered.\n\n\nI need to find a different issue. Let me check #56186 - it has a UI config error preservation fix that's only 1 file with minimal changes. Or maybe I should just let the existing PRs handle these straightforward issues and focus on something that requires more actual code changes. The real question is whether I can meaningfully improve on what's already been submitted. I'm realizing the existing PRs already cover these issues pretty thoroughly, so I should focus on finding something that actually needs our contribution rather than duplicating work that's already in progress.\n\nLet me shift tactics and look for an issue that doesn't have a corresponding PR yet—something small enough for a first contribution but substantive enough to matter. I'll scan through the open issues to identify what hasn't been addressed.","thinkingSignature":"56a816bf978ebff5d31228c9f29e6b46365ca8cc0435ab2c1c3b19667c6622fa"},{"type":"text","text":"已有多个 PR 处理同样的问题。让我找一个还没有 PR 修复的真实 bug。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_4w6gfy1anqy8_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue list --repo openclaw/openclaw --state open --limit 50 --search \"label:bug -label:security\" --json number,title,labels,comments --jq '.[] | select(.comments == 0) | {number,title,labels:[.labels