{"type":"message","id":"8564c01d","parentId":"dde1c799","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:47:44.233Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There are lots of bugs without PRs. But I need to find one that's:1. Small enough (XS/S)2. Well understood by us\n3. Actually fixable without deep expertise in that area\n\nLooking at the list:\n- #56338: \"Feishu's requireMention=false is invalid\" - this is a Feishu issue, we have some context\n- #56226: hooks.mappings[].channel rejects valid plugins - we supported #56247 for this\n- #56161: skills install ignores current workspace - we supported #56243 for this\n\nLet me look for something that:1. Is in our familiar territory (Feishu, hooks, multi-agent)\n\n\n2. Has no PR yet\n3. Is small\n\nI'm noticing a pattern in the newer issues - there are several Feishu-related bugs that appear multiple times across different time periods, which makes sense given their recency. Let me dig into #56338 specifically to understand what's actually happening with the requireMention validation.\n\nI should also check #56197 since it involves Feishu token refresh logic, which is more substantial than a simple boolean fix. The #56219 Telegram regression is worth investigating too, though I need to understand the scope better. Let me start with the smaller, well-defined issues first - #56388 about isolated cron sessions and Telegram config looks promising as a focused problem to tackle. I'm also seeing #56338 about Feishu's requireMention validation, which seems like another contained issue to evaluate.\n\nLet me pull the details on #56338 and #56197 to understand what needs fixing.","thinkingSignature":"9a3f6aa342b7563b7f489c319d33c423d3fe34d5402d72c187a0a077afe0b9af"},{"type":"text","text":"#56338（Feishu requireMention=false invalid）和 #56197（Feishu 401 token refresh）这两个值得研究。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_scvyfmam8qtj_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue view 56338 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json number,title,body,labels --jq '{number,title,labels:[.labels[].name],body}'\necho \"===\"\ngh issue view 56197 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json number,title,body,labels --jq '{number,title,labels:[.labels[].name],body}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":68329,"output":458,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":91412,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702046681,"responseId":"061700de1acd8e99f0a4c69b609d849f"}}
{"type":"message","id":"b3239d64","parentId":"8564c01d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:47:45.112Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_scvyfmam8qtj_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nFeishu tested the following configuration and found that setting `requireMention=false` had no effect. Within groups, `@feishu_bot` was still required for a response; the bot only read and did not reply.\\n\\n```\\n    \\\"feishu\\\": {\\n      \\\"enabled\\\": true,\\n      \\\"dmPolicy\\\": \\\"pairing\\\",\\n      \\\"groupPolicy\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"groupAllowFrom\\\": [\\n          \\\"oc_xxxxxx\\\", \\n          \\\"oc_yyyyyy\\\"\\n       ],\\n      \\\"groups\\\": {\\n        \\\"oc_xxxxxx\\\": {\\n          \\\"allowFrom\\\": [\\\"ou_12313131\\\"],\\n          \\\"requireMention\\\": false\\n        },\\n....\\n```\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\nAs described above\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nI hope I can reply to messages without using @bots.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nAs described above\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24.04\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\ndocker\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nminimax\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nminimax\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56338,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Feishu's requireMention=false is invalid.\"}\n===\n{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nFeishu embedded agent returns raw HTTP 401 \\\"Invalid token\\\" error to user instead of retrying with refreshed token\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1.Configure Feishu as a messaging channel with model routing through AutoGLM proxy (zai provider)\\n2.Wait for the model API's JWT token to expire (or start a new session when the token is near expiry)\\n3.Send any message from the Feishu client\\n4.The bot replies with \\\"HTTP 401: Invalid token\\\"\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nThe embedded agent should detect the 401, trigger a token refresh, and retry the request. At minimum, it should not surface the raw HTTP error message to the end user.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nThe 401 error is passed directly as the reply text to the Feishu user. Logs show the token refresh (config reload) occurs after the error has already been returned. The webchat session recovers after refresh, but the Feishu embedded agent continues to fail intermittently on subsequent requests.\\n\\n[feishu] received message from ou_cb34... (p2p)\\n[feishu] dispatching to agent (session=agent:main:feishu:direct:ou_cb34...)\\n[pi-ai] request POST .../chat/completions status=401\\n[agent/embedded] embedded run agent end: isError=true error=HTTP 401: \\\"Invalid token\\\"\\n[feishu] dispatch complete (queuedFinal=true, replies=1)\\n[reload] config change detected; evaluating reload (models.providers.zai.models)\\n[reload] config change applied\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.2.25\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nWindows 10 (x64)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Model\\n\\npony-alpha-2 (GLM-5-Turbo)\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nzai → autoglm-api.zhipuai.cn/autoclaw-proxy/proxy/autoclaw\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56197,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Feishu embedded agent returns HTTP 401 \\\"Invalid token\\\" to user instead of retrying with refreshed token\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":846,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nFeishu tested the following configuration and found that setting `requireMention=false` had no effect. Within groups, `@feishu_bot` was still required for a response; the bot only read and did not reply.\\n\\n```\\n    \\\"feishu\\\": {\\n      \\\"enabled\\\": true,\\n      \\\"dmPolicy\\\": \\\"pairing\\\",\\n      \\\"groupPolicy\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n      \\\"groupAllowFrom\\\": [\\n          \\\"oc_xxxxxx\\\", \\n          \\\"oc_yyyyyy\\\"\\n       ],\\n      \\\"groups\\\": {\\n        \\\"oc_xxxxxx\\\": {\\n          \\\"allowFrom\\\": [\\\"ou_12313131\\\"],\\n          \\\"requireMention\\\": false\\n        },\\n....\\n```\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\nAs described above\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nI hope I can reply to messages without using @bots.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nAs described above\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24.04\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\ndocker\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nminimax\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nminimax\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56338,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Feishu's requireMention=false is invalid.\"}\n===\n{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nFeishu embedded agent returns raw HTTP 401 \\\"Invalid token\\\" error to user instead of retrying with refreshed token\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1.Configure Feishu as a messaging channel with model routing through AutoGLM proxy (zai provider)\\n2.Wait for the model API's JWT token to expire (or start a new session when the token is near expiry)\\n3.Send any message from the Feishu client\\n4.The bot replies with \\\"HTTP 401: Invalid token\\\"\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nThe embedded agent should detect the 401, trigger a token refresh, and retry the request. At minimum, it should not surface the raw HTTP error message to the end user.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nThe 401 error is passed directly as the reply text to the Feishu user. Logs show the token refresh (config reload) occurs after the error has already been returned. The webchat session recovers after refresh, but the Feishu embedded agent continues to fail intermittently on subsequent requests.\\n\\n[feishu] received message from ou_cb34... (p2p)\\n[feishu] dispatching to agent (session=agent:main:feishu:direct:ou_cb34...)\\n[pi-ai] request POST .../chat/completions status=401\\n[agent/embedded] embedded run agent end: isError=true error=HTTP 401: \\\"Invalid token\\\"\\n[feishu] dispatch complete (queuedFinal=true, replies=1)\\n[reload] config change detected; evaluating reload (models.providers.zai.models)\\n[reload] config change applied\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.2.25\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nWindows 10 (x64)\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Model\\n\\npony-alpha-2 (GLM-5-Turbo)\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nzai → autoglm-api.zhipuai.cn/autoclaw-proxy/proxy/autoclaw\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56197,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Feishu embedded agent returns HTTP 401 \\\"Invalid token\\\" to user instead of retrying with refreshed token\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774702065093}}
{"type":"message","id":"e2b5ce36","parentId":"b3239d64","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:48:04.049Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"#56338 is about Feishu's `requireMention=false` not working - it's a regression where without mention, the bot reads but doesn't reply. This is a routing/policy issue.\n\n#56197 is about the Feishu embedded agent returning 401 \"Invalid token\" to user instead of refreshing token and retrying.\n\nBoth are interesting but:\n- #56338: Might be in the routing logic, could be complex to trace\n- #56197: The token refresh happens AFTER the error is already returned - the fix would be to retry before surfacing the error\n\nLet me think about which one I can actually fix with minimal code change:\n\n\n- #56197 requires catching the 401 in the Feishu embedded agent and triggering a token refresh before retrying - this seems more straightforward to locate in the code\n- #56338 is about `requireMention=false` being ignored, which could be in the routing/policy check logic\n\nGiven my time constraints, I should pick one and start exploring the codebase to understand how the routing logic works and where this bug might be hiding.\n\nActually, #56219 about the Telegram plugin failing to load is likely a regression that's already been addressed in recent PRs. Let me focus on #56197 instead - the core issue is that when the token expires, the agent returns a 401 error instead of silently refreshing and retrying, so I need to find where HTTP errors are being handled in the Feishu integration and add retry logic there. I'm wondering if the problem is actually in the embedded agent rather than the Feishu plugin itself—the token refresh happens after the error surfaces, which suggests the API call is being made without a valid token in the first place. This could be a zai/AutoGLM proxy configuration issue, but the real fix might belong in the plugin's request handler to validate tokens before making the API call.\n\nLooking at what I can actually fix with a small PR, I should probably focus on the Feishu `requireMention=false` regression since that's more straightforward, or revisit one of the simpler issues like the Feishu tool re-registration or hook channel validation problems.\n\nBut I need to be realistic about my constraints—I'm working with a shallow clone so I can't easily search the codebase. Instead, I should look for something like the Telegram regression where I can identify the problem from the description alone and write a fix targeting a specific file I can reference. The most practical move is probably to examine what the existing PRs have already done for these issues and either build on those solutions or spot where they might be incomplete.","thinkingSignature":"b9c87315bfac9722e30a7064e663e726b88fe333c410b048ea10acccdc7c3714"},{"type":"text","text":"#56197 比较有挑战性但价值高——Feishu embedded agent 返回原始 401 给用户而不是先刷新 token 再重试。这个修复逻辑清晰：捕获 401，检查是否 token 失效，触发 refresh 后 retry。\n\n让我找一下 Feishu embedded agent 的请求处理代码。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_tm25etzny4tz_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu -name \"*.ts\" | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":69722,"output":636,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":92983,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702065113,"responseId":"061700f1b78b5f813531f463b8c33605"}}
