u/src/send-result.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/chat-schema.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/monitor.bot-menu.lifecycle.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/card-ux-launcher.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/monitor.reply-once.lifecycle.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/monitor.acp-init-failure.lifecycle.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/monitor.webhook-security.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/setup-surface.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/media.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/probe.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/perm-schema.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/monitor.card-action.lifecycle.test.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/channel.runtime.ts\n/root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/card-ux-shared.ts","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774702084083}}
{"type":"message","id":"a4016ad2","parentId":"3c6a34de","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:48:27.462Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the Feishu extension files. The embedded agent would be in the inbound/dispatch flow. Let me look for the agent dispatch/invoke code in the Feishu extension.\n\nActually, looking at the issue description more carefully:\n- The issue says \"Feishu embedded agent\" \n- The logs show: `[pi-ai] request POST .../chat/completions status=401`\n- `[agent/embedded] embedded run agent end: isError=true error=HTTP 401: \"Invalid token\"`\n\nThe \"embedded agent\" is the pi-ai plugin or similar. The Feishu channel is just the transport. The 401 error comes from the AI provider (zai/AutoGLM proxy), not from Feishu itself.\n \nThe logs reveal the real problem: the 401 error gets returned to the user before the token refresh happens. The config reload that should prevent this is occurring too late. Since this involves the zai provider's AutoGLM proxy, it's not something I can directly fix in the Feishu channel code itself.\n\nLet me reconsider the issue more carefully. The embedded agent runs through the pi-ai plugin, which calls the AI provider and gets a 401 response. Instead of retrying with a refreshed token, it surfaces the error directly to the user. The fix needs to be in the pi-ai plugin's request handling layer. But this is getting complex. Maybe I should look at something simpler instead.\n\nActually, I think the real issue is that when the token expires, the API call fails with 401, and only after that does the config reload refresh the token. The sequence is: API call → 401 error surfaced to user → config reload triggers. What should happen instead is the embedded agent should detect the 401, trigger a token refresh, then retry the request. The timing shows the config reload (token refresh) happens after the error response, which suggests the token was already expired when the request was made. I need to find where the embedded agent makes HTTP calls to the AI provider and add retry logic with automatic token refresh on 401 responses.\n\nLooking at this differently, the actual problem is simpler than I'm making it—the 401 error shouldn't be exposed to users at all. The embedded agent should either refresh the token and retry silently, or return a user-friendly error message. Since this requires understanding the pi-ai plugin architecture which I don't have visibility into, I should look for a different issue that's more straightforward to address.\n\nLet me explore the Feishu requireMention issue instead, or better yet, find a PR that already has a fix in place and help move it forward. The #56219 Telegram regression is recent and has a clear description—maybe I can find a straightforward fix there.\n\nActually, I should step back. The real bottleneck isn't finding the right issue—it's that I need to either understand the codebase deeply enough to fix it or work with issues I've already analyzed. The #56338 Feishu requireMention=false regression is worth investigating since Feishu routing is familiar territory, but I should be realistic about what's achievable here.","thinkingSignature":"fa55689166a82abf874071cf65cdc92d40180af9470a6e339865e63074b35c17"},{"type":"text","text":"\n#56197 的问题涉及 pi-ai embedded agent 的 HTTP 调用层，需要深入理解 provider 层的 token refresh 机制，比较复杂。让我换一个更明确的——看 #56338（requireMention=false regression），这个问题在 Feishu routing 逻辑里，比较容易定位。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_331287no67nx_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src -name \"*.ts\" | xargs grep -l \"requireMention\\|require_mention\" 2>/dev/null | head -10"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":70753,"output":757,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":94135,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702084108,"resp