{"type":"message","id":"5ca10234","parentId":"6c8af98e","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:49:43.674Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `resolveFeishuGroupConfig` function looks correct. It looks up the group config by exact match first, then case-insensitive match, then falls back to wildcard `*`.\n\nSo the group config lookup should work. The issue might be elsewhere.\n\nWait - let me re-read the issue more carefully:\n\n```\n\"groups\": {\n  \"oc_xxxxxx\": {\n    \"allowFrom\": [\"ou_12313131\"],\n    \"requireMention\": false\n  }\n}\n```\n\nAnd the `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy` is called with:\n```typescript\n({ requireMention } = resolveFeishuReplyPolicy({\n  isDirectMessage: false,\n  globalConfig: feishuCfg,\n  groupConfig,\n}));\n```\n\nIf `groupConfig` is correctly resolved (with `requireMention: false`), then the result should be `{ requireMention: false }`.\n\nThen:\n```typescript\nif (requireMention && !ctx.mentionedBot) {\n  // skip\n}\n```\n\nIf `requireMention` is `false`, this condition is `false`, so we DON'T skip. This is correct.\n\nBUT - there might be ANOTHER check earlier that skips the message before we even get to this point!\n\nLet me look at the full flow in bot.ts more carefully. The message might be skipped by an earlier check.\n\nActually, looking at line 361:\n```typescript\nif (isGroup) {\n```\n\nAnd then within that block, there's a lot of logic. Maybe there's something before line 415 that causes the message to be skipped?\n\nOr maybe the issue is that the message is being processed but the response is not being sent because of a different issue.\n\nLet me look at what happens AFTER the requireMention check. If `requireMention=false` and `!ctx.mentionedBot` is true (user didn't mention bot), then:\n```typescript\nconst route = resolveAgentRoute({...});\n...\nconst shouldSuppress = ctx.mentionedBot || !requireMention ? normalizeAgentId(route.agentId) : null;\n```\n\nIf `requireMention=false` and the user didn't mention the bot, then `!requireMention` is `true`, so `shouldSuppress` gets set to the normalized agent ID instead of null. This means the response gets suppressed when it shouldn't be.\n\nBut hold on - if `requireMention=false`, I need to trace through the condition more carefully. When `ctx.mentionedBot` is false and `requireMention` is false, the expression `ctx.mentionedBot || !requireMention` evaluates to `false || true` which is `true`, so `shouldSuppress` is NOT null. That means the message IS being suppressed when it should be delivered.\n\nSo the real problem is: the condition is backwards. When mention isn't required, we shouldn't suppress the response just because the bot wasn't mentioned. The logic needs to change so that `shouldSuppress` is only set when mention IS required AND the bot wasn't mentioned. Now I'm re-examining the original issue—the bot reads messages but only responds when @mentioned. So `requireMention=false` should let it respond without an @mention, yet it only reads. This suggests either the config isn't being applied correctly, or there's a policy check blocking responses before the routing logic even runs. Let me trace through what happens after `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy` at line 415 to see where the response is actually being suppressed.","thinkingSignature":"0785768b70f7ede7916563596c929a2e9ad91761a8232a5c6eea8dea5d1825c8"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_t4ec97i89l10_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '360,400p' /root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/bot.ts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":75335,"output":745,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98705,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702163508,"responseId":"061701531332956335d9be27a8983d14"}}
{"type":"message","id":"0c8236b1","parentId":"5ca10234","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:49:43.721Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_t4ec97i89l10_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"let requireMention = false; // DMs never require mention; groups may override below\n  if (isGroup) {\n    if (groupConfig?.enabled === false) {\n      log(`feishu[${account.accountId}]: group ${ctx.chatId} is disabled`);\n      return;\n    }\n    const defaultGroupPolicy = resolveDefaultGroupPolicy(cfg);\n    const { groupPolicy, providerMissingFallbackApplied } = resolveOpenProviderRuntimeGroupPolicy({\n      providerConfigPresent: cfg.channels?.feishu !== undefined,\n      groupPolicy: feishuCfg?.groupPolicy,\n      defaultGroupPolicy,\n    });\n    warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce({\n      providerMissingFallbackApplied,\n      providerKey: \"feishu\",\n      accountId: account.accountId,\n      log,\n    });\n    const groupAllowFrom = feishuCfg?.groupAllowFrom ?? [];\n    // DEBUG: log(`feishu[${account.accountId}]: groupPolicy=${groupPolicy}`);\n\n    // Check if this GROUP is allowed (groupAllowFrom contains group IDs like oc_xxx, not user IDs)\n    const groupAllowed = isFeishuGroupAllowed({\n      groupPolicy,\n      allowFrom: groupAllowFrom,\n      senderId: ctx.chatId, // Check group ID, not sender ID\n      senderName: undefined,\n    });\n\n    if (!groupAllowed) {\n      log(\n        `feishu[${account.accountId}]: group ${ctx.chatId} not in groupAllowFrom (groupPolicy=${groupPolicy})`,\n      );\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Sender-level allowlist: per-group allowFrom takes precedence, then global groupSenderAllowFrom\n    const perGroupSenderAllowFrom = groupConfig?.allowFrom ?? [];\n    const globalSenderAllowFrom = feishuCfg?.groupSenderAllowFrom ?? [];\n    const effectiveSenderAllowFrom =\n      perGroupSenderAllowFrom.length > 0 ? perGroupSenderAllowFrom : globalSenderAllowFrom;"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":15,"aggregated":"let requireMention = false; // DMs never require mention; groups may override below\n  if (isGroup) {\n    if (groupConfig?.enabled === false) {\n      log(`feishu[${account.accountId}]: group ${ctx.chatId} is disabled`);\n      return;\n    }\n    const defaultGroupPolicy = resolveDefaultGroupPolicy(cfg);\n    const { groupPolicy, providerMissingFallbackApplied } = resolveOpenProviderRuntimeGroupPolicy({\n      providerConfigPresent: cfg.channels?.feishu !== undefined,\n      groupPolicy: feishuCfg?.groupPolicy,\n      defaultGroupPolicy,\n    });\n    warnMissingProviderGroupPolicyFallbackOnce({\n      providerMissingFallbackApplied,\n      providerKey: \"feishu\",\n      accountId: account.accountId,\n      log,\n    });\n    const groupAllowFrom = feishuCfg?.groupAllowFrom ?? [];\n    // DEBUG: log(`feishu[${account.accountId}]: groupPolicy=${groupPolicy}`);\n\n    // Check if this GROUP is allowed (groupAllowFrom contains group IDs like oc_xxx, not user IDs)\n    const groupAllowed = isFeishuGroupAllowed({\n      groupPolicy,\n      allowFrom: groupAllowFrom,\n      senderId: ctx.chatId, // Check group ID, not sender ID\n      senderName: undefined,\n    });\n\n    if (!groupAllowed) {\n      log(\n        `feishu[${account.accountId}]: group ${ctx.chatId} not in groupAllowFrom (groupPolicy=${groupPolicy})`,\n      );\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Sender-level allowlist: per-group allowFrom takes precedence, then global groupSenderAllowFrom\n    const perGroupSenderAllowFrom = groupConfig?.allowFrom ?? [];\n    const globalSenderAllowFrom = feishuCfg?.groupSenderAllowFrom ?? [];\n    const effectiveSenderAllowFrom =\n      perGroupSenderAllowFrom.length > 0 ? perGroupSenderAllowFrom : globalSenderAllowFrom;","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774702183703}}
{"type":"message","id":"f476f581","parentId":"0c8236b1","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:49:54.100Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see a potential issue! Look at lines 379-384:\n\n```typescript\nconst groupAllowed = isFeishuGroupAllowed({\n  groupPolicy,\n  allowFrom: groupAllowFrom,  // This is feishuCfg.groupAllowFrom, NOT groupConfig.allowFrom!\n  senderId: ctx.chatId,\n  senderName: undefined,\n});\n```\n\nThe `isFeishuGroupAllowed` check uses `feishuCfg.groupAllowFrom` (global level), NOT `groupConfig.allowFrom` (per-group level)! \n\nBut wait, there IS per-group allowFrom handling right below:\n\n\n```typescript\nconst perGroupSenderAllowFrom = groupConfig?.allowFrom ?? [];\nconst globalSenderAllowFrom = feishuCfg?.groupSenderAllowFrom ?? [];\n```\n\nSo the sender-level check uses per-group first, then falls back to global. That's fine.\n\nThe group-level check at line 379 uses `groupAllowFrom` (which is `feishuCfg.groupAllowFrom`). But `groupAllowFrom` in Feishu config is for ALLOWING GROUP IDS, not for per-group config. The issue might be that when `groupPolicy` is set but there's no explicit `groupAllowFrom` configured, the logic doesn't properly evaluate whether the group should be allowed.\n\nLet me look at `isFeishuGroupAllowed` to see how it actually handles the group policy and allowlist check.","thinkingSignature":"59dbeba7fddcd5b9f5db99640f121fad95dace419939e78478d155f021ccdc9c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_75dhyd1is67z_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '90,115p' /root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/policy.ts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":76502,"output":340,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":99467,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702183723,"responseId":"06170167ce0474efeb277e828ae3b8e3"}}
