{"type":"message","id":"ea0bd4c4","parentId":"8b7d8d61","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:50:36.288Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No recent commits to bot.ts in the Feishu extension. This suggests the regression might not be in the Feishu plugin itself, but in a shared/core component that the Feishu plugin depends on.\n\nLet me look at the issue description more carefully again. The user says:\n> setting `requireMention=false` had no effect. Within groups, `@feishu_bot` was still required for a response\n\nThis is very clear. `requireMention=false` at the group level is being ignored. The bot only reads but does not reply.\n\nLet me think about what could cause this:\n1. The `requireMention` value from config is not being picked up - maybe the schema validation strips it out\n\n\n2. The `requireMention` value IS picked up but the check is wrong somewhere\n3. The message is being processed but the reply is not sent for a different reason\n\nWait - I just realized something important. The issue says the bot \"only reads but does not reply\". This is different from \"the bot ignores messages\". If the bot IS reading messages (and logging them), then the message IS being received. But the reply is not being sent.\n\nIf `requireMention=false` and the user didn't mention the bot, the condition `if (requireMention && !ctx.mentionedBot)` evaluates to `false`, so we shouldn't skip. But maybe the issue is that `ctx.mentionedBot` is incorrectly being set to `true` even when the user didn't mention the bot?\n\nLooking at the code more carefully:\n```typescript\nconst shouldSuppress = ctx.mentionedBot || !requireMention ? normalizeAgentId(route.agentId) : null;\n```\n\nThis is confusing - if `requireMention=false`, then `!requireMention` is `true`, so `shouldSuppress` gets set to the agent ID (suppress the reply), which would actually cause the bot NOT to reply. That seems backwards from what we'd want.\n\nActually wait, let me think about what `shouldSuppress` being set means. If it's set to a value, the reply gets suppressed. So when `requireMention=false` and the user didn't mention the bot, we're setting `shouldSuppress` to the agent ID, which would suppress the reply entirely. That's the opposite of what `requireMention=false` should do. I think I see the issue now - the ternary operator logic appears to be inverted. When mention isn't required, it should suppress the response, but the current code is doing the opposite. If I invert the condition to `!ctx.mentionedBot && requireMention`, then `shouldSuppress` would correctly be null when no mention is needed, allowing the response through.","thinkingSignature":"7ee0b4762acf9587e0fa46f7f92c892ba733190dc4af69894be079d036d4393d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8ijoewzew5di_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"shouldSuppress\\|mentionedBot\" /root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/bot.ts | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":77970,"output":601,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":101196,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702219422,"responseId":"0617018b89b1b7124a2c68560b72c01f"}}
