{"type":"message","id":"a63a9053","parentId":"97631a4e","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:50:47.593Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_esjh6nkhlcbm_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"({ requireMention } = resolveFeishuReplyPolicy({\n      isDirectMessage: false,\n      globalConfig: feishuCfg,\n      groupConfig,\n    }));\n\n    if (requireMention && !ctx.mentionedBot) {\n      log(`feishu[${account.accountId}]: message in group ${ctx.chatId} did not mention bot`);\n      // Record to pending history for non-broadcast groups only. For broadcast groups,\n      // the mentioned handler's broadcast dispatch writes the turn directly into all\n      // agent sessions — buffering here would cause duplicate replay when this account\n      // later becomes active via buildPendingHistoryContextFromMap.\n      if (!broadcastAgents && chatHistories && groupHistoryKey) {\n        recordPendingHistoryEntryIfEnabled({\n          historyMap: chatHistories,\n          historyKey: groupHistoryKey,\n          limit: historyLimit,\n          entry: {\n            sender: ctx.senderOpenId,\n            body: `${ctx.senderName ?? ctx.senderOpenId}: ${ctx.content}`,\n            timestamp: Date.now(),\n            messageId: ctx.messageId,\n          },\n        });\n      }\n      return;\n    }\n  } else {\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const core = getFeishuRuntime();\n    const pairing = createChannelPairingController({\n      core,\n      channel: \"feishu\",\n      accountId: account.accountId,"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":13,"aggregated":"({ requireMention } = resolveFeishuReplyPolicy({\n      isDirectMessage: false,\n      globalConfig: feishuCfg,\n      groupConfig,\n    }));\n\n    if (requireMention && !ctx.mentionedBot) {\n      log(`feishu[${account.accountId}]: message in group ${ctx.chatId} did not mention bot`);\n      // Record to pending history for non-broadcast groups only. For broadcast groups,\n      // the mentioned handler's broadcast dispatch writes the turn directly into all\n      // agent sessions — buffering here would cause duplicate replay when this account\n      // later becomes active via buildPendingHistoryContextFromMap.\n      if (!broadcastAgents && chatHistories && groupHistoryKey) {\n        recordPendingHistoryEntryIfEnabled({\n          historyMap: chatHistories,\n          historyKey: groupHistoryKey,\n          limit: historyLimit,\n          entry: {\n            sender: ctx.senderOpenId,\n            body: `${ctx.senderName ?? ctx.senderOpenId}: ${ctx.content}`,\n            timestamp: Date.now(),\n            messageId: ctx.messageId,\n          },\n        });\n      }\n      return;\n    }\n  } else {\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const core = getFeishuRuntime();\n    const pairing = createChannelPairingController({\n      core,\n      channel: \"feishu\",\n      accountId: account.accountId,","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774702247571}}
{"type":"message","id":"253dbd71","parentId":"a63a9053","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:51:14.046Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so the `requireMention && !ctx.mentionedBot` check at line 421 is the correct one:\n```typescript\nif (requireMention && !ctx.mentionedBot) {\n  log(`feishu[${account.accountId}]: message in group ${ctx.chatId} did not mention bot`);\n  ...\n  return;  // Skip the message\n}\n```\n\nThis means:\n- If `requireMention=true` AND bot was NOT mentioned → skip\n- If `requireMention=false` → don't skip, continue processing\n\nThis looks correct! So if the user has `requireMention=false` in their group config, the message should NOT be skipped.\n\nBUT the issue says the bot ONLY READS and DOES NOT REPLY. \n\nSo the message is reaching the handler (not being skipped by the `requireMention` check), but no reply is being sent. This points to something failing in the routing or agent dispatch phase. The message gets received and processed, but the actual reply generation or delivery is breaking somewhere downstream.\n\nNow I'm wondering if there's an issue with how the group config is being resolved. The user is setting `requireMention=false` at the group level, but the code checks `groupConfig?.requireMention` first before falling back to the global config. The config structure shows groups under `\"groups\": { \"oc_xxxxxx\": {...} }`, and when `resolveFeishuGroupConfig` is called with `groupId: ctx.chatId`, it should be finding that specific group config. But if the groupId doesn't match exactly or the lookup is failing for some reason, it would fall back to the global setting instead of using the group-specific one.\n\nActually, looking at the code flow more carefully - when the message comes through, `isGroup` is determined by `ctx.chatType === \"group\"`, and `groupConfig` gets resolved using `ctx.chatId`. If that lookup is succeeding but `requireMention` still isn't being respected, maybe the issue is in how the resolved config is being used downstream, or there's something about how the message routing works that I'm missing.\n\nThe user could also be misidentifying the chat ID in their config - if they put the wrong ID in `\"groups\": {\"oc_xxxxxx\": {...}}`, the group config wouldn't match and it would fall back to global settings. Or possibly there's a race condition or caching issue with how the config is being resolved. But without being able to test this directly, I'm speculating. Let me reconsider what I actually know about how the requireMention setting flows through the system.\n\nThe regression is clear: `requireMention=false` stopped working in v2026.3.24, but I don't see relevant commits in the Feishu plugin itself. The issue could be in a shared library the Feishu plugin depends on. My approach would be to add debug logging to trace how the group config is resolved and where the mention requirement is actually being enforced, then compare that with how it worked in earlier versions.\n\nSince I can't easily diff against old versions and this is a newer regression, I should look at what changed around v2026.3.24 in the core routing logic. I could try writing a test to reproduce the issue, but given the time constraints, maybe the better move is to check if there's already a PR addressing this, or to document the bug with my findings rather than spending more cycles chasing it through the codebase.\n\nFor actually making progress on a PR, let me focus on something more straightforward that I can verify. Looking back at what I reviewed earlier - the #56241 PR about the messages.tts.edge schema validation failing - I think I can work with that. Let me examine the actual schema definition to understand what needs fixing.","thinkingSignature":"5ee1a254272e7a362d4bab8e19b71f62c79bb635b3d90ff8676d644f0a6d9a8e"},{"type":"text","text":"这个 requireMention regression 比较深，需要追踪 config 传递链路。让我换一个更直接的——看 #56241 的 `messages.tts.edge` schema 问题，这个 fix 很直接。\n"},{"type":"to