{"type":"message","id":"b65d0b00","parentId":"2f46c821","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:53:00.707Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue now! \n\nThe `MessagesSchema` (line 147-188) has `.strict()` at line 188 (`.strict().optional()`). This means the `messages` object STRICTLY only allows the keys defined in the schema, and rejects any unknown keys.\n\nBut wait - `tts: TtsConfigSchema` IS one of the defined keys. And `TtsConfigSchema` includes `edge: TtsMicrosoftConfigSchema`. So `messages.tts.edge` should be valid.\n\nUnless... let me look at whether there's something specific about the `tts` field that makes it reject `edge`.\n\nWait, let me look at the `tts: TtsConfigSchema` at line 188 more carefully. The `TtsConfigSchema` is NOT wrapped with `.optional()`. \n\nSo the real problem is that the `messages` object itself is marked as optional with `.strict()`, which means the entire `messages` key can be absent, but if it's present, it must contain only the defined keys and the `tts` field becomes required within it. The `tts` field is required, not optional. If a user provides `messages: { tts: { edge: {...} } }`, it should work. But the issue description mentions \"Config validation rejects `messages.tts.edge` as an unrecognized key\" — which means the validation is somehow treating `edge` as an unknown field within the `tts` object, even though it's defined in `TtsConfigSchema`. I'm realizing the schema structure itself might be the issue rather than the `edge` field being missing. Looking at how `TtsMicrosoftConfigSchema` is defined with `.strict()` and `.optional()`, it seems like the `edge` key should be accepted if it's defined in the schema. Let me trace through whether `messages.tts.edge` is actually present in the TtsConfigSchema or if there's a mismatch between what the types declare and what the schema validation actually allows.\n\nI'm going in circles here. The PR #56241 claims to fix this by adding explicit tests for edge TTS configuration, which suggests the schema might actually be working but there's a test gap rather than a code problem. Rather than keep digging through the schema definitions, I should just look at what changed in the PR itself to understand the actual fix.","thinkingSignature":"db9c7242a063c80fa8936ee7f92e24a503627478d8a7484ae07bf16fd3f0adb7"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_omldtie2uovb_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56241 --jq '.body' 2>/dev/null | head -60"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":86106,"output":531,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":109262,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702362622,"responseId":"0617021ae130e381afd554446b030ba9"}}
{"type":"message","id":"2628a222","parentId":"b65d0b00","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:53:01.333Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_omldtie2uovb_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Issue\nCloses #56220\n\nConfig validation rejects `messages.tts.edge` as an unrecognized key, but documentation and TypeScript types still declare it as supported.\n\n## Changes\nAdded explicit tests to verify that `TtsConfigSchema` accepts the legacy `messages.tts.edge` configuration key. This ensures:\n\n1. The `edge` field is properly validated in the TTS config schema\n2. All edge TTS configuration options are supported (voice, lang, outputFormat, pitch, rate, volume, saveSubtitles, proxy, timeoutMs)\n3. Existing configurations using edge TTS settings continue to work\n\n## Tests\n- Added test for edge field with basic voice configuration\n- Added test for edge field with all configuration options\n\nAll tests pass.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Tests added\n- [x] Tests pass\n- [x] Minimal change focused on the issue"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":555,"aggregated":"## Issue\nCloses #56220\n\nConfig validation rejects `messages.tts.edge` as an unrecognized key, but documentation and TypeScript types still declare it as supported.\n\n## Changes\nAdded explicit tests to verify that `TtsConfigSchema` accepts the legacy `messages.tts.edge` configuration key. This ensures:\n\n1. The `edge` field is properly validated in the TTS config schema\n2. All edge TTS configuration options are supported (voice, lang, outputFormat, pitch, rate, volume, saveSubtitles, proxy, timeoutMs)\n3. Existing configurations using edge TTS settings continue to work\n\n## Tests\n- Added test for edge field with basic voice configuration\n- Added test for edge field with all configuration options\n\nAll tests pass.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Tests added\n- [x] Tests pass\n- [x] Minimal change focused on the issue","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isEr