{"type":"message","id":"98b3906e","parentId":"b1f7a5f9","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:02:52.265Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_bc1n41vyy1tq_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"Fixes #53636\\n\\n## Problem\\nWhen saving channel config fails, the error message was lost after loadChannels refresh, leaving users without feedback on what went wrong.\\n\\n## Solution\\nPreserve the error state before calling loadConfig/loadChannels, then restore it to channelsError after the refresh completes.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- ui/src/ui/app-channels.ts: Save lastError before refresh, restore to channelsError after\\n\\n## Branch Info\\n- Created from: upstream/main (2026-03-28)\\n- Commits: 1\\n- Replaces: previous #53636 (closed)\",\"number\":56186,\"title\":\"fix(ui): preserve config save error after loadChannels refresh (#53636)\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":824,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"Fixes #53636\\n\\n## Problem\\nWhen saving channel config fails, the error message was lost after loadChannels refresh, leaving users without feedback on what went wrong.\\n\\n## Solution\\nPreserve the error state before calling loadConfig/loadChannels, then restore it to channelsError after the refresh completes.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- ui/src/ui/app-channels.ts: Save lastError before refresh, restore to channelsError after\\n\\n## Branch Info\\n- Created from: upstream/main (2026-03-28)\\n- Commits: 1\\n- Replaces: previous #53636 (closed)\",\"number\":56186,\"title\":\"fix(ui): preserve config save error after loadChannels refresh (#53636)\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774702972242}}
{"type":"message","id":"4f2ba49d","parentId":"98b3906e","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:03:05.284Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"#56186 is a UI fix - preserving config save error after loadChannels refresh. This is XS, clean fix, easy to understand. Let me look at the actual code to understand the issue and write my own PR for this or a similar simple issue.\n\nActually wait - the issue is for `ui/src/ui/app-channels.ts` which is in the `ui/` directory. My fork clone has `ui/` directory? Let me check.Actually, many of these small fixes are already being worked on by other people. I need to find one that hasn't been claimed yet.\n\nLet me look for issues that:\n1. Have no PR yet\n\n\n2. Are XS/S size\n3. Are in code areas I understand\n\nThe Feishu `requireMention=false` issue (#56338) is a good candidate - I was analyzing it earlier. But actually, looking at the config, it seems like the config IS being passed correctly to `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy`. The issue is more complex - might be in how the result is used. Let me look for something simpler. Actually, let me look at #56219 - Telegram plugin fails to load after upgrade to 2026.3.27. This is regression, clear description.\n\nActually, let me think about what would be a good PR to write. \n\nI should focus on Feishu routing since that's what I know best. The `requireMention=false` issue is interesting, but let me start with something more straightforward - #56341 about the `message_sent` typed hook not firing for Telegram channel delivery.","thinkingSignature":"fb29ea8d0d9b2895e565b0b5da69642a33d775190551de47d94a4152d0f0a87d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2coqvqrfmqah_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue view 56341 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json number,title,body,labels --jq '{number,title,labels:[.labels[].name],body}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":77807,"output":382,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":100814,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702972267,"responseId":"0617047ce741ad102042ca06affe5c45"}}
{"type":"message","id":"6e1bac05","parentId":"4f2ba49d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:03:05.809Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_2coqvqrfmqah_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nPlugin-registered message_sent typed hooks do not fire when messages are delivered via Telegram. The message_received hook fires    correctly for inbound messages, but message_sent never triggers for outbound Telegram replies.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n# Telegram Plugin Hook Issue\\n\\n**Problem:** Plugin-registered `message_sent` typed hooks do not fire when messages are delivered via Telegram. The `message_received` hook fires correctly for inbound messages, but `message_sent` never triggers for outbound Telegram replies.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Create a plugin with kind: `\\\"memory\\\"` that registers a `message_sent` hook:\\n   ```javascript\\n   api.on(\\\"message_sent\\\", async (event) =\\u003e {\\n     console.log(\\\"message_sent fired\\\"); // never prints\\n   }, { name: \\\"my-hook\\\" });\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nmessage_sent should fire after the agent's reply is delivered via Telegram, consistent with the docs at /automation/hooks which list message:sent as firing \\\"when an outbound message is successfully sent.\\\"\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\n  - message_received — fires ✓\\n  - before_agent_start — fires ✓\\n  - message_sent — never fires ✗\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\nnpm global\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nqwen3.5 9b\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nollama\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56341,\"title\":\"[Bug]: message_sent typed hook not firing for Telegram channel delivery (v2026.3.24)\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":479,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nBehavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nPlugin-registered message_sent typed hooks do not fire when messages are delivered via Telegram. The message_received hook fires    correctly for inbound messages, but message_sent never triggers for outbound Telegram replies.\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n# Telegram Plugin Hook Issue\\n\\n**Problem:** Plugin-registered `message_sent` typed hooks do not fire when messages are delivered via Telegram. The `message_received` hook fires correctly for inbound messages, but `message_sent` never triggers for outbound Telegram replies.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Create a plugin with kind: `\\\"memory\\\"` that registers a `message_sent` hook:\\n   ```javascript\\n   api.on(\\\"message_sent\\\", async (event) =\\u003e {\\n     console.log(\\\"message_sent fired\\\"); // never prints\\n   }, { name: \\\"my-hook\\\" });\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nmessage_sent should fire after the agent's reply is delivered via Telegram, consistent with the docs at /automation/hooks which list message:sent as firing \\\"when an outbound message is successfully sent.\\\"\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\n  - message_received — fires ✓\\n  - before_agent_start — fires ✓\\n  - message_sent — never fires ✗\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\n2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nUbuntu 24\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\nnpm global\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nqwen3.5 9b\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nollama\\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56341,\"title\":\"[Bug]: message_sent typed hook not firing for Telegram channel delivery (v2026.3.24)\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774702985787}}
