{"type":"message","id":"8771b61e","parentId":"e739ece9","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:04:38.992Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The NO_REPLY fix hasn't been applied to the fork yet (it's still based on main). So the fix in #56167 is needed.\n\nActually, let me just write a PR for a Feishu issue I understand well. Let me look at the Feishu requireMention issue again, but this time focus on finding the actual bug in the code.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach. Let me look at the `channels` config for Feishu and see if there's a schema issue.\n\nActually, you know what, let me just focus on finding a really simple fix. Let me look at the issue list again and find something that's:\n\n\n1. A clear bug with a clear fix\n2. In code I can understand quickly\n3. Has no PR yet\n\nThe #56338 requireMention issue is actually a good candidate because I know the Feishu routing code. Let me dig into it more carefully this time. The issue says requireMention=false has no effect and the bot still requires @mention. But in the config shown, there's `dmPolicy: \"pairing\"` and `groupPolicy: \"open\"` along with specific group allowFrom entries, so the problem might be in how these policies interact with the mention requirement.\n\nLooking at the bot.ts logic, `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy` is called with `isDirectMessage: false` for groups, and requireMention should default to false when not explicitly set. But the reporter is saying requireMention=false isn't being respected. Let me trace through what `groupConfig` actually contains when it's passed to `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy` — it's coming from `resolveFeishuGroupConfig`, which looks up the group configuration by ID.\n\nThe issue might be that the group config isn't being found at all, so it falls back to undefined, or the allowFrom check is failing before we even get to the mention check. Actually, I think I see it now — when `groupPolicy: \"open\"` is set without any explicit groups configuration, the bot might still be enforcing mentions because the fallback logic isn't handling the \"open\" policy correctly. I'm tracing through the early return conditions in the code - there's a return when the group is disabled, another when the group isn't in the allowFrom list, and a third when the message doesn't mention the bot and mentions are required. But in this case, `requireMention=false` should mean that third check passes, so the message shouldn't be rejected. Let me look at the actual config structure to understand where the group-specific settings are being read from.\n\nActually, I think the real issue might be with how the config is being parsed - the reporter has a `groups` block with group-specific `requireMention` settings, but the schema validation might not be recognizing `requireMention` as a valid field, so it's being silently stripped out during parsing. I need to verify whether `requireMention` is actually defined in the FeishuGroupConfig schema.","thinkingSignature":"9c19d00633139d1a192e65cbc735bd5b199f326fc778eac84f2d155e7ef1bb9e"},{"type":"text","text":"让我直接找个简单清晰的 bug 来修。看看 Feishu group config schema 里 `requireMention` 字段的类型定义。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_vxlsr6cs6vhc_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"requireMention\\|FeishuGroupConfig\" /root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/config-schema.ts | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":83376,"output":687,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":106688,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703056268,"responseId":"061704d0a363ee432c9e63e55e1d6fcb"}}
