{"type":"message","id":"bc1d617c","parentId":"4e8285a2","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:04:43.092Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_l65l47j7pqf4_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"encryptKey: buildSecretInputSchema().optional(),\n    verificationToken: buildSecretInputSchema().optional(),\n    domain: FeishuDomainSchema.optional().default(\"feishu\"),\n    connectionMode: FeishuConnectionModeSchema.optional().default(\"websocket\"),\n    webhookPath: z.string().optional().default(\"/feishu/events\"),\n    ...FeishuSharedConfigShape,\n    dmPolicy: DmPolicySchema.optional().default(\"pairing\"),\n    reactionNotifications: ReactionNotificationModeSchema.optional().default(\"own\"),\n    groupPolicy: GroupPolicySchema.optional().default(\"allowlist\"),\n    requireMention: z.boolean().optional().default(true),\n    groupSessionScope: GroupSessionScopeSchema,\n    topicSessionMode: TopicSessionModeSchema,\n    // Dynamic agent creation for DM users\n    dynamicAgentCreation: DynamicAgentCreationSchema,\n    // Optimization flags\n    typingIndicator: z.boolean().optional().default(true),\n    resolveSenderNames: z.boolean().optional().default(true),\n    // Multi-account configuration\n    accounts: z.record(z.string(), FeishuAccountConfigSchema.optional()).optional(),\n  })\n  .strict()\n  .superRefine((value, ctx) => {\n    const defaultAccount = value.defaultAccount?.trim();\n    if (defaultAccount && value.accounts && Object.keys(value.accounts).length > 0) {\n      const normalizedDefaultAccount = normalizeAccountId(defaultAccount);\n      if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(value.accounts, normalizedDefaultAccount)) {\n        ctx.addIssue({\n          code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,\n          path: [\"defaultAccount\"],\n          message: `channels.feishu.defaultAccount=\"${defaultAccount}\" does not match a configured account key`,\n        });\n      }\n    }\n\n    const defaultConnectionMode = value.connectionMode ?? \"websocket\";\n    const defaultVerificationTokenConfigured = hasConfiguredSecretInput(value.verificationToken);"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":11,"aggregated":"encryptKey: buildSecretInputSchema().optional(),\n    verificationToken: buildSecretInputSchema().optional(),\n    domain: FeishuDomainSchema.optional().default(\"feishu\"),\n    connectionMode: FeishuConnectionModeSchema.optional().default(\"websocket\"),\n    webhookPath: z.string().optional().default(\"/feishu/events\"),\n    ...FeishuSharedConfigShape,\n    dmPolicy: DmPolicySchema.optional().default(\"pairing\"),\n    reactionNotifications: ReactionNotificationModeSchema.optional().default(\"own\"),\n    groupPolicy: GroupPolicySchema.optional().default(\"allowlist\"),\n    requireMention: z.boolean().optional().default(true),\n    groupSessionScope: GroupSessionScopeSchema,\n    topicSessionMode: TopicSessionModeSchema,\n    // Dynamic agent creation for DM users\n    dynamicAgentCreation: DynamicAgentCreationSchema,\n    // Optimization flags\n    typingIndicator: z.boolean().optional().default(true),\n    resolveSenderNames: z.boolean().optional().default(true),\n    // Multi-account configuration\n    accounts: z.record(z.string(), FeishuAccountConfigSchema.optional()).optional(),\n  })\n  .strict()\n  .superRefine((value, ctx) => {\n    const defaultAccount = value.defaultAccount?.trim();\n    if (defaultAccount && value.accounts && Object.keys(value.accounts).length > 0) {\n      const normalizedDefaultAccount = normalizeAccountId(defaultAccount);\n      if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(value.accounts, normalizedDefaultAccount)) {\n        ctx.addIssue({\n          code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,\n          path: [\"defaultAccount\"],\n          message: `channels.feishu.defaultAccount=\"${defaultAccount}\" does not match a configured account key`,\n        });\n      }\n    }\n\n    const defaultConnectionMode = value.connectionMode ?? \"websocket\";\n    const defaultVerificationTokenConfigured = hasConfiguredSecretInput(value.verificationToken);","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774703083069}}
{"type":"message","id":"7e777015","parentId":"bc1d617c","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:04:48.170Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Line 224 shows `requireMention: z.boolean().optional().default(true)` at the TOP LEVEL of the FeishuConfig. This is a global setting for Feishu. But the reporter has `requireMention` inside `groups.oc_xxxxxx.requireMention`. Let me check the FeishuGroupConfigSchema.","thinkingSignature":"1281365e0a3effbeb7768393946e837245ddd322ea910277865bd9db0c570b84"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_gbjh9jzxvekl_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '130,175p' /root/openclaw-fork/extensions/feishu/src/config-schema.ts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":84632,"output":116,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":107373,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703083095,"responseId":"061704eba693ec6490dfc2bde922af63"}}
{"type":"message","id":"51b5d410","parentId":"7e777015","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:04:48.218Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_gbjh9jzxvekl_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * Reply-in-thread mode for group chats.\n * - \"disabled\" (default): Bot replies are normal inline replies\n * - \"enabled\": Bot replies create or continue a Feishu topic thread\n *\n * When enabled, the Feishu reply API is called with `reply_in_thread: true`,\n * causing the reply to appear as a topic (话题) under the original message.\n */\nconst ReplyInThreadSchema = z.enum([\"disabled\", \"enabled\"]).optional();\n\nexport const FeishuGroupSchema = z\n  .object({\n    requireMention: z.boolean().optional(),\n    tools: ToolPolicySchema,\n    skills: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n    enabled: z.boolean().optional(),\n    allowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n    systemPrompt: z.string().optional(),\n    groupSessionScope: GroupSessionScopeSchema,\n    topicSessionMode: TopicSessionModeSchema,\n    replyInThread: ReplyInThreadSchema,\n  })\n  .strict();\n\nconst FeishuSharedConfigShape = {\n  webhookHost: z.string().optional(),\n  webhookPort: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n  capabilities: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n  markdown: MarkdownConfigSchema,\n  configWrites: z.boolean().optional(),\n  dmPolicy: DmPolicySchema.optional(),\n  allowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n  groupPolicy: GroupPolicySchema.optional(),\n  groupAllowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n  groupSenderAllowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n  requireMention: z.boolean().optional(),\n  groups: z.record(z.string(), FeishuGroupSchema.optional()).optional(),\n  historyLimit: z.number().int().min(0).optional(),\n  dmHistoryLimit: z.number().int().min(0).optional(),\n  dms: z.record(z.string(), DmConfigSchema).optional(),\n  textChunkLimit: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n  chunkMode: z.enum([\"length\", \"newline\"]).optional(),\n  blockStreamingCoalesce: BlockStreamingCoalesceSchema,\n  mediaMaxMb: z.number().positive().optional(),\n  httpTimeoutMs: z.number().int().positive().max(300_000).optional(),"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":12,"aggregated":"/**\n * Reply-in-thread mode for group chats.\n * - \"disabled\" (default): Bot replies are normal inline replies\n * - \"enabled\": Bot replies create or continue a Feishu topic thread\n *\n * When enabled, the Feishu reply API is called with `reply_in_thread: true`,\n * causing the reply to appear as a topic (话题) under the original message.\n */\nconst ReplyInThreadSchema = z.enum([\"disabled\", \"enabled\"]).optional();\n\nexport const FeishuGroupSchema = z\n  .object({\n    requireMention: z.boolean().optional(),\n    tools: ToolPolicySchema,\n    skills: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n    enabled: z.boolean().optional(),\n    allowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n    systemPrompt: z.string().optional(),\n    groupSessionScope: GroupSessionScopeSchema,\n    topicSessionMode: TopicSessionModeSchema,\n    replyInThread: ReplyInThreadSchema,\n  })\n  .strict();\n\nconst FeishuSharedConfigShape = {\n  webhookHost: z.string().optional(),\n  webhookPort: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n  capabilities: z.array(z.string()).optional(),\n  markdown: MarkdownConfigSchema,\n  configWrites: z.boolean().optional(),\n  dmPolicy: DmPolicySchema.optional(),\n  allowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n  groupPolicy: GroupPolicySchema.optional(),\n  groupAllowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n  groupSenderAllowFrom: z.array(z.union([z.string(), z.number()])).optional(),\n  requireMention: z.boolean().optional(),\n  groups: z.record(z.string(), FeishuGroupSchema.optional()).optional(),\n  historyLimit: z.number().int().min(0).optional(),\n  dmHistoryLimit: z.number().int().min(0).optional(),\n  dms: z.record(z.string(), DmConfigSchema).optional(),\n  textChunkLimit: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n  chunkMode: z.enum([\"length\", \"newline\"]).optional(),\n  blockStreamingCoalesce: BlockStreamingCoalesceSchema,\n  mediaMaxMb: z.number().positive().optional(),\n  httpTimeoutMs: z.number().int().positive().max(300_000).optional(),","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774703088196}}
{"type":"message","id":"31892ae8","parentId":"51b5d410","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:05:16.923Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so the schema looks correct:\n- `FeishuGroupSchema` has `requireMention: z.boolean().optional()` \n- `FeishuSharedConfigShape` also has `requireMention: z.boolean().optional()` at the global level\n- `groups: z.record(z.string(), FeishuGroupSchema.optional()).optional()` allows per-group config\n\nAnd in `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy`:\n```typescript\nconst requireMention =\n    params.groupConfig?.requireMention ?? params.globalConfig?.requireMention ?? true;\n```\n\nThis should correctly use the group-level `requireMention` if set, otherwise fall back to global, otherwise default to `true`.\n\n\nThe issue description mentions that `requireMention=false` had no effect even though it's set in the group configuration, but the logic appears sound. There might be a regression in v2026.3.24 where the group config isn't being retrieved properly, or the schema has a `.strict()` validation that's rejecting the field. Let me trace through `resolveFeishuGroupConfig` to see if the group-level settings are actually being resolved.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the group config requires `enabled: true` (or undefined) to be processed at all—if `enabled` is false, the handler returns early. But in the reporter's case, `requireMention=false` is set under the group, not `enabled`, so that shouldn't be blocking it. The issue might be something else entirely, maybe in how the config is being parsed or validated.\n\nLooking at the reported config structure with `groupPolicy: \"open\"` and the bot still requiring mentions despite `requireMention=false`, I'm wondering if the group config lookup itself is failing. Let me trace through `resolveFeishuGroupConfig` to see if it's actually finding and returning the group-specific config correctly.\n\nWait, I think I found it—in `bot.ts` around line 361, there's a check for `if (isGroup)` that runs `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy` to determine if mentions are required. But there's a logic issue in `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy` where it returns early for direct messages with `requireMention: false`, and then falls through to check `params.groupConfig?.requireMention` which might not be set correctly for groups.\n\nActually, let me trace through the issue more carefully. The reporter is saying that even when they set `requireMention=false` in the group config, the bot still requires a mention. But if `resolveFeishuReplyPolicy` is being called correctly, it should return `false` for groups where `requireMention=false` is configured. This makes me think the problem might not be in this function at all—it could be that the message is being rejected before it even reaches the reply policy check, possibly due to a sender allowlist issue or something earlier in the pipeline.\n\nLooking at the actual config the reporter provided, the group `oc_xxxxxx` has `allowFrom: [\"ou_12313131\"]` set, but the message is coming from a different user. If that user isn't in the allowlist, the message would be rejected before we even get to the `requireMention` logic. That would explain why the setting appears to have no effect—the message is being filtered out at the access control layer, not the mention requirement layer. I'm probably overcomplicating this. The real issue might be something entirely different—maybe the Telegram channel doesn't support the same mention detection that Feishu does, or the hook system has a gap that only manifests in specific scenarios. Rather than chase my tail on this, I should just pick one of the simpler confirmed bugs and write a fix for it instead.\n\nLooking at what's available, the Feishu `requireMention=false` issue is actually well-documented with a clear reproduction case, and I understand the routing logic well enough to attempt a fix. Let me start by creating a test case that reproduces the bug, then work backward to find and fix the underlying cause.","thinkingSignature":"6c5cecb92b5a0492424ff4e0df90188e42f68a61e21e35bdfb1becafddb212dd"},{"type":"text","text":"Feishu schema 结构清晰，`requireMention=false` 应该可以工作。让我找一个更直接可复现的 bug 来写 PR。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_v45bxmap1vki_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue view 56388 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json number,title,body --jq '{number,title,body}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":85266,"output":893,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":108784,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703088221,"responseId":"061704f0c0c420b128f46a53bdbd9be3"}}
{"type":"message","id":"05579f6d","parentId":"31892ae8","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:05:17.829Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_v45bxmap1vki_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nAfter a gateway restart (including those triggered by openclaw gateway restart or an npm update), isolated cron sessions fail to deliver messages to Telegram with the errorThe main session continues to work fine (Telegram shows as ON/OK in openclaw status). Only isolated cron sessions are affected. A second gateway restart resolves the issue temporarily, but it recurs after the next gateway restart or updateError: Outbound not configured for channel: telegram\\n\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Have one or more isolated cron jobs configured to deliver via Telegram\\n2. Restart the gateway (openclaw gateway restart or update via npm)\\n3. Wait for a cron to fire — delivery fails with the above error\\n4. Run openclaw gateway restart again — delivery resumes working\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nIsolated cron sessions should inherit the Telegram outbound config correctly after a gateway restart without requiring a second restart.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nIsolated cron sessions lose Telegram outbound config after gateway restart/update\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\nRunning 2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nmoc os sequoia 15.7.4\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\ninstalled\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nsonnet 4.5\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nopen claw \\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"number\":56388,\"title\":\"[Bug]:Isolated cron sessions lose Telegram outbound config after gateway restart/update\"}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":862,"aggregated":"{\"body\":\"### Bug type\\n\\nRegression (worked before, now fails)\\n\\n### Beta release blocker\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nAfter a gateway restart (including those triggered by openclaw gateway restart or an npm update), isolated cron sessions fail to deliver messages to Telegram with the errorThe main session continues to work fine (Telegram shows as ON/OK in openclaw status). Only isolated cron sessions are affected. A second gateway restart resolves the issue temporarily, but it recurs after the next gateway restart or updateError: Outbound not configured for channel: telegram\\n\\n\\n### Steps to reproduce\\n\\n1. Have one or more isolated cron jobs configured to deliver via Telegram\\n2. Restart the gateway (openclaw gateway restart or update via npm)\\n3. Wait for a cron to fire — delivery fails with the above error\\n4. Run openclaw gateway restart again — delivery resumes working\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nIsolated cron sessions should inherit the Telegram outbound config correctly after a gateway restart without requiring a second restart.\\n\\n### Actual behavior\\n\\nIsolated cron sessions lose Telegram outbound config after gateway restart/update\\n\\n### OpenClaw version\\n\\nRunning 2026.3.24\\n\\n### Operating system\\n\\nmoc os sequoia 15.7.4\\n\\n### Install method\\n\\ninstalled\\n\\n### Model\\n\\nsonnet 4.5\\n\\n### Provider / routing chain\\n\\nopen claw \\n\\n### Additional provider/model setup details\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Logs, screenshots, and evidence\\n\\n```shell\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Impact and severity\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional information\\n\\n_No response_\",\"number\":56388,\"title\":\"[Bug]:Isolated cron sessions lose Telegram outbound config after gateway restart/update\"}","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774703117807}}
{"type":"message","id":"54f487df","parentId":"05579f6d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:05:31.020Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a cron/telegram regression - after gateway restart, isolated cron sessions lose Telegram outbound config. The error is \"Outbound not configured for channel: telegram\". This is a second-restart workaround scenario.\n\nLet me look for where in the cron delivery code the Telegram outbound config is initialized. But this involves understanding the cron session isolation mechanism and how outbound config is passed.\n\nActually, let me find something even simpler. Let me look for an issue that's specifically about a missing/null check bug - those are usually easy one-liners.Let me try a completely different approach: look at what code has changed recently that could have caused a regression, and write a fix for that.\n\n\nThe Telegram plugin loading failure after upgrade is probably the quickest win here - the issue description is straightforward and it affects a single file, so the fix should be contained.","thinkingSignature":"c53d3126c63a6c16519677e3330fda3126c69d1bacbc716004d747b7709f9a71"},{"type":"text","text":"#56219（升级后 Telegram 插件加载失败）更明确——让我直接看代码。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_b3rys56gom25_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue view 56219 --repo openclaw/openclaw --json number,title,body,labels --jq '{number,title,labels:[.labels[].name],body}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":84506,"output":250,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":107381,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703117832,"responseId":"0617050ed3c1faabc0cc4d649afeacb8"}}
