{"type":"message","id":"f3a6855f","parentId":"37c69b06","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:12:00.430Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me look at what the actual bug is. The issue #56220 says \"Config schema rejects legacy messages.tts.edge while docs/types still say it is supported.\" Let me check the types.tts.ts file to see if `edge` is declared there.","thinkingSignature":"a4270c2d24304493e76bef56563425f15a7db8671d986dc44b4eed4c2a69a029"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ujcmpofg0w0h_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/openclaw-fork/src/config/types.tts.ts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":65234,"output":91,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":87950,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703513679,"responseId":"06170699e9d5465e06aa68e46c874fcc"}}
{"type":"message","id":"9b9441c6","parentId":"f3a6855f","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:12:00.483Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_ujcmpofg0w0h_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { SecretInput } from \"./types.secrets.js\";\n\nexport type TtsProvider = string;\n\nexport type TtsMode = \"final\" | \"all\";\n\nexport type TtsAutoMode = \"off\" | \"always\" | \"inbound\" | \"tagged\";\n\nexport type TtsModelOverrideConfig = {\n  /** Enable model-provided overrides for TTS. */\n  enabled?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided TTS text blocks. */\n  allowText?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided provider override (default: false). */\n  allowProvider?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided voice/voiceId override. */\n  allowVoice?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided modelId override. */\n  allowModelId?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided voice settings override. */\n  allowVoiceSettings?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided normalization or language overrides. */\n  allowNormalization?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided seed override. */\n  allowSeed?: boolean;\n};\n\nexport type TtsProviderConfigMap = Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>;\n\nexport type LegacyTtsConfigCompat = {\n  /** Legacy ElevenLabs configuration. Prefer providers.elevenlabs. */\n  elevenlabs?: {\n    apiKey?: SecretInput;\n    baseUrl?: string;\n    voiceId?: string;\n    modelId?: string;\n    seed?: number;\n    applyTextNormalization?: \"auto\" | \"on\" | \"off\";\n    languageCode?: string;\n    voiceSettings?: {\n      stability?: number;\n      similarityBoost?: number;\n      style?: number;\n      useSpeakerBoost?: boolean;\n      speed?: number;\n    };\n  };\n  /** Legacy OpenAI configuration. Prefer providers.openai. */\n  openai?: {\n    apiKey?: SecretInput;\n    baseUrl?: string;\n    model?: string;\n    voice?: string;\n    /** Playback speed (0.25–4.0, default 1.0). */\n    speed?: number;\n    /** System-level instructions for the TTS model (gpt-4o-mini-tts only). */\n    instructions?: string;\n  };\n  /** Legacy alias for Microsoft speech configuration. Prefer providers.microsoft. */\n  edge?: {\n    /** Explicitly allow Microsoft speech usage (no API key required). */\n    enabled?: boolean;\n    voice?: string;\n    lang?: string;\n    outputFormat?: string;\n    pitch?: string;\n    rate?: string;\n    volume?: string;\n    saveSubtitles?: boolean;\n    proxy?: string;\n    timeoutMs?: number;\n  };\n  /** Legacy Microsoft speech configuration. Prefer providers.microsoft. */\n  microsoft?: {\n    enabled?: boolean;\n    voice?: string;\n    lang?: string;\n    outputFormat?: string;\n    pitch?: string;\n    rate?: string;\n    volume?: string;\n    saveSubtitles?: boolean;\n    proxy?: string;\n    timeoutMs?: number;\n  };\n};\n\nexport type TtsConfig = LegacyTtsConfigCompat & {\n  /** Auto-TTS mode (preferred). */\n  auto?: TtsAutoMode;\n  /** Legacy: enable auto-TTS when `auto` is not set. */\n  enabled?: boolean;\n  /** Apply TTS to final replies only or to all replies (tool/block/final). */\n  mode?: TtsMode;\n  /** Primary TTS provider (fallbacks are automatic). */\n  provider?: TtsProvider;\n  /** Optional model override for TTS auto-summary (provider/model or alias). */\n  summaryModel?: string;\n  /** Allow the model to override TTS parameters. */\n  modelOverrides?: TtsModelOverrideConfig;\n  /** Provider-specific TTS settings keyed by speech provider id. */\n  providers?: TtsProviderConfigMap;\n  /** Optional path for local TTS user preferences JSON. */\n  prefsPath?: string;\n  /** Hard cap for text sent to TTS (chars). */\n  maxTextLength?: number;\n  /** API request timeout (ms). */\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":10,"aggregated":"import type { SecretInput } from \"./types.secrets.js\";\n\nexport type TtsProvider = string;\n\nexport type TtsMode = \"final\" | \"all\";\n\nexport type TtsAutoMode = \"off\" | \"always\" | \"inbound\" | \"tagged\";\n\nexport type TtsModelOverrideConfig = {\n  /** Enable model-provided overrides for TTS. */\n  enabled?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided TTS text blocks. */\n  allowText?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided provider override (default: false). */\n  allowProvider?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided voice/voiceId override. */\n  allowVoice?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided modelId override. */\n  allowModelId?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided voice settings override. */\n  allowVoiceSettings?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided normalization or language overrides. */\n  allowNormalization?: boolean;\n  /** Allow model-provided seed override. */\n  allowSeed?: boolean;\n};\n\nexport type TtsProviderConfigMap = Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>;\n\nexport type LegacyTtsConfigCompat = {\n  /** Legacy ElevenLabs configuration. Prefer providers.elevenlabs. */\n  elevenlabs?: {\n    apiKey?: SecretInput;\n    baseUrl?: string;\n    voiceId?: string;\n    modelId?: string;\n    seed?: number;\n    applyTextNormalization?: \"auto\" | \"on\" | \"off\";\n    languageCode?: string;\n    voiceSettings?: {\n      stability?: number;\n      similarityBoost?: number;\n      style?: number;\n      useSpeakerBoost?: boolean;\n      speed?: number;\n    };\n  };\n  /** Legacy OpenAI configuration. Prefer providers.openai. */\n  openai?: {\n    apiKey?: SecretInput;\n    baseUrl?: string;\n    model?: string;\n    voice?: string;\n    /** Playback speed (0.25–4.0, default 1.0). */\n    speed?: number;\n    /** System-level instructions for the TTS model (gpt-4o-mini-tts only). */\n    instructions?: string;\n  };\n  /** Legacy alias for Microsoft speech configuration. Prefer providers.microsoft. */\n  edge?: {\n    /** Explicitly allow Microsoft speech usage (no API key required). */\n    enabled?: boolean;\n    voice?: string;\n    lang?: string;\n    outputFormat?: string;\n    pitch?: string;\n    rate?: string;\n    volume?: string;\n    saveSubtitles?: boolean;\n    proxy?: string;\n    timeoutMs?: number;\n  };\n  /** Legacy Microsoft speech configuration. Prefer providers.microsoft. */\n  microsoft?: {\n    enabled?: boolean;\n    voice?: string;\n    lang?: string;\n    outputFormat?: string;\n    pitch?: string;\n    rate?: string;\n    volume?: string;\n    saveSubtitles?: boolean;\n    proxy?: string;\n    timeoutMs?: number;\n  };\n};\n\nexport type TtsConfig = LegacyTtsConfigCompat & {\n  /** Auto-TTS mode (preferred). */\n  auto?: TtsAutoMode;\n  /** Legacy: enable auto-TTS when `auto` is not set. */\n  enabled?: boolean;\n  /** Apply TTS to final replies only or to all replies (tool/block/final). */\n  mode?: TtsMode;\n  /** Primary TTS provider (fallbacks are automatic). */\n  provider?: TtsProvider;\n  /** Optional model override for TTS auto-summary (provider/model or alias). */\n  summaryModel?: string;\n  /** Allow the model to override TTS parameters. */\n  modelOverrides?: TtsModelOverrideConfig;\n  /** Provider-specific TTS settings keyed by speech provider id. */\n  providers?: TtsProviderConfigMap;\n  /** Optional path for local TTS user preferences JSON. */\n  prefsPath?: string;\n  /** Hard cap for text sent to TTS (chars). */\n  maxTextLength?: number;\n  /** API request timeout (ms). */\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774703520463}}
{"type":"message","id":"8158729a","parentId":"9b9441c6","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:12:23.749Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see that `edge` IS defined in the TypeScript types file (`types.tts.ts`):\n```typescript\nedge?: {\n  /** Legacy alias for Microsoft speech configuration. Prefer providers.microsoft. */\n  enabled?: boolean;\n  voice?: string;\n  ...\n}\n```And in `zod-schema.core.ts`, the `TtsConfigSchema` uses:\n```typescript\nedge: TtsMicrosoftConfigSchema,\nmicrosoft: TtsMicrosoftConfigSchema,\n```Both `edge` and `microsoft` map to `TtsMicrosoftConfigSchema`. This looks correct in the current codebase.\n\nSo the issue #56220 might have been fixed already in the latest version. \n\nThe PR #56241 adds tests to verify `edge` works, which suggests the schema currently accepts it—but if those tests are passing while the issue claims validation rejects it, either the fix is already in place or the issue was opened before the correction was made. Looking at the current code structure, `edge` maps to `TtsMicrosoftConfigSchema`, so this might already be resolved.\n\nNow I'm shifting focus entirely. Instead of hunting through issues for the perfect PR opportunity, I should think about what I actually know well—Feishu routing, multi-agent systems, message hooks—and either write documentation improvements or tackle something genuinely XS and isolated in those areas. The core problem is that most of these bugs are either too complex, already claimed, or not actually reproducible without specific setups.\n\nLet me step back and look at the practical constraints: I can support existing PRs, review code, and investigate issues, but writing a PR from scratch requires actually understanding and fixing something. The most honest move is to focus on those three things rather than forcing a PR that doesn't naturally emerge from my actual expertise.","thinkingSignature":"a98bd4f05c988d525852f8354959f51409b0991e06be7c232e67966d65325e95"},{"type":"text","text":"好，找 bug 写 PR 这条路走不通了——要么已有 PR 在修，要么 bug 太深。让我换个策略：**直接帮已有的 PR 作者完成代码审查和支持**。\n\nxixi 之前超时是因为 gh 命令的 jq 管道太复杂。让我给 xixi 设计一个更简单的任务：找到还没人 review 的 S 级 PR。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8wwlkcwd7fjb_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr list --repo openclaw/openclaw --state open --limit 50 --search \"is:pr no:reviews reviewDecision:pending size:S\" --json number,title,author,reviewDecision --jq '.[] | {number,title,author:.author.login}' 2>/dev/null | head -40"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":63048,"output":520,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86193,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703520491,"responseId":"061706a0cabb37fc15f7cb71c212622a"}}
