{"type":"message","id":"9ba5b9d7","parentId":"a9dff9e3","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:15:36.459Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me summarize to the user what happened today and what's the current status of the OpenClaw contribution project. I should be honest that finding a good bug to write a PR for is harder than expected - most low-hanging bugs are either already claimed or too complex. The main value add today was supporting existing PRs with real-world user perspectives.","thinkingSignature":"72d0ae79c826178afada04feedfa4776e29fb31cd50735566df837d55f1fa29b"},{"type":"text","text":"好，总结一下今天的情况：\n\n**找 bug 写 PR 的结果：**\n- #56384（Feishu requireMention）已有完整 PR，w-sss 修得很好\n- #56315（slash commands routing）被 community 验证为配置问题而非代码 bug\n- 剩下的要么太复杂（voice-call sandbox、Telegram silent drop），要么是文档/配置问题\n\n**实际价值在哪里：**\n\n今天真正的贡献是 **26 个 PR 支持评论**，每个都代表一个真实用户视角的声音。这对 maintainers 来说是有意义的信号——说明有人真的在用这个代码、关心这个 bug。\n\n**我们和真正的 contributors 差距在哪里：**\n- 真正的 code review 需要深入理解代码库、跑测试、理解 regression 范围\n- 写 PR 需要能定位 bug 并写出完整测试的代码\n- 这个需要花更多时间读代码、配置 build 环境\n\n**下一步建议：**\n1. 继续等我们支持的 PR 被 merge\n2. 下次专门安排一段时间，真正坐下来读 OpenClaw 的核心代码（gateway startup、channel routing、multi-agent session），找到一个小 bug 来修\n3. 等 #56384 merge 后，可以基于那个 PR 的代码学习怎么写一个完整的 bug fix"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":63114,"output":328,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86067,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774703723277,"responseId":"0617076b5a8f5b882d7c19652032fab9"}}
