{"type":"message","id":"15555a06","parentId":"b4691743","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:16:29.385Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No new PRs created since our last scan. Let me now try to push our fork to origin. Wait - we rebased our fork to upstream/main, but our origin is EronFan/openclaw-fork which is 1900 commits behind. If we push, we'll force push and overwrite the origin. That's fine since it's our own fork.\n\nActually wait - \"ahead of 'origin/main' by 1900 commits\" - that's the rebase effect. Our local branch now has all the upstream commits plus our local changes (none). We should force push to our origin to keep it in sync.\n\nBut actually, let me think about whether we need to push. The goal was to write PRs, not maintain a fork. \n\nLet me focus on what we actually need to do. I'll check if there's a simpler bug I can tackle - something in the Feishu plugin where I understand the context well enough. That Feishu NO_REPLY token fix we supported earlier is still unmerged, so I could try writing something similar. The issue is that our fork is rebased to upstream/main, but since we didn't actually make any code changes, pushing would just be redundant anyway.\n\nLet me focus on the actual work instead - finding a small bug to fix and preparing a PR.","thinkingSignature":"afcf83ad1db54f0feb9871e05956b7cff61773ae860585e269b81f123dee4fbf"},{"type":"text","text":"没有新 PR。趁这段时间，看看有没有我们熟悉领域的小 bug。Feishu outbound NO_REPLY token 泄露那个我们支持过，看看能不能找到类似的简单修复。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_jufogvur7wds_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -rn \"NO_REPLY\\|isSilentReplyText\" /root/openclaw-fork/src/ --include=\"*.ts\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"test\\|\\.d\\.ts\" | head -10"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":77415,"output":370,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":100410,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopRea