{"type":"message","id":"1f70b879","parentId":"e3e5593c","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:17:25.859Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"None of the PRs we supported have gotten a maintainer review yet. This is expected - maintainers are busy and these PRs are all relatively new. Let me now think about what else I can do productively.\n\nThe key insight is: we've been very active supporting PRs, but we haven't written any code ourselves. For the goal of getting into the top 20 contributors, supporting PRs counts less than writing code.\n\nLet me think about whether there's something simple I can code and PR:\n1. The Feishu NO_REPLY fix (#56167) is already done by Talegqz\n2. The Feishu requireMention fix (#56384) is already done by w-sss\n\n\n3. Many of the XS fixes we supported are already done\n\nWhat I should do is look at the Feishu plugin and see if there's a small gap that hasn't been addressed yet. Since we understand the Feishu routing and channel structure, maybe there's a minor bug in the Feishu plugin that would be a good first PR attempt. Even just submitting a well-documented issue with a proposed fix could be valuable. But actually, the best use of my time right now is probably to keep supporting the community - commenting on good PRs helps maintainers prioritize and gets our name recognized as a serious contributor.\n\nHowever, looking back at the MEMO the user sent, the goal is clearly to write code and get PRs merged. So I need to shift focus and find something code-related. Let me explore whether there's a straightforward bug in the Feishu plugin I could fix, or if I should just pick up one of the smaller issues that's already been reported and submit a PR for that.","thinkingSignature":"0bead1ce9556cbf7ba8e5bd56ea0e40a922d54caab56139da8e5cb2b69f04d64"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_fhe466gvb207_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh issue list --repo openclaw/openclaw --state open --limit 20 --search \"created:>2026-03-27 label:bug -label:security no:pr\" --json number,title,labels --jq '.[] | {number,title,labels:[.labels[].name]}' 2>/dev/null | head -50"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79057,"output":442,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":102124,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703829852,"responseId":"061707d612510090fae0161a36026269"}}
{"type":"message","id":"90a3da14","parentId":"1f70b879","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:17:26.465Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_fhe466gvb207_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56399,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Discord WebSocket crash — `Max reconnect attempts (0)` kills gateway process\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56388,\"title\":\"[Bug]:Isolated cron sessions lose Telegram outbound config after gateway restart/update\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56377,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Device pairing gets stuck after macOS minor update because paired device metadata pins old OS version\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:crash\"],\"number\":56374,\"title\":\"[Bug]:\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56371,\"title\":\"[Bug]: WebUI message deletion is not persistent — deleted messages reappear after new message\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56369,\"title\":\"[Bug]: gateway:startup hook fires before channel adapters are ready — message tool fails silently\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56367,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Voice-call plugin ignores agents.defaults.sandbox.mode: \\\"off\\\" - forces Docker sandbox for voice lane responses\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:behavior\"],\"number\":56341,\"title\":\"[Bug]: message_sent typed hook not firing for Telegram channel delivery (v2026.3.24)\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"bug:crash\"],\"number\":56339,\"title\":\"Discord health-monitor stale-socket restart causes uncaught exception that crashes the entire gateway\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56338,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Feishu's requireMention=false is invalid.\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56321,\"title\":\"[Bug]: @openclaw/whatsapp not avaliable on NPM\"}\n{\"labels\":[\"bug\",\"regression\"],\"number\":56315,\"title\":\"[Bug]: Slash commands (/reset, /status, /reasonin