{"type":"message","id":"5f1f5ad4","parentId":"90a3da14","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:17:41.966Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"These are all bug regression issues that we've seen before. Most of these already have PRs fixing them or are too complex to fix quickly.\n\nLet me think about what I can do with the remaining time. I should:\n1. Push our fork to origin (though this isn't critical)\n2. Continue to scan for new PRs\n3. Maybe write a test case for something\n\nActually, let me think about #56371 - WebUI message deletion not persistent. This might be a simple bug where the deletion state isn't being saved. Let me check if there's already a PR for this.\n\nActually, the key realization is: we've been spending a lot of time supporting other people's PRs, which is valuable for reputation but doesn't directly help us write code. \n\nI should probably try to write a real PR myself, even something small like adding a test case that demonstrates a bug. Let me look at the most active contributors to the repo to understand what quality contributions look like - w-sss seems to be very active with many XS/S PRs around config, cron, and feishu. I could try fixing one of the simpler issues like #56186 or #56241 that are already identified, or find something else straightforward to contribute.\n\nLooking at #56241 - fixing the config schema that rejects edge TTS - seems like the most approachable path since it involves just schema changes and tests without deep routing logic. But I should first understand why the schema is rejecting messages.tts.edge if the types.tts.ts clearly defines it as a valid field. Let me check the issue to see if there's already a PR addressing this.","thinkingSignature":"87480575303104cb36d370108ecfcb50527a0fbfe029ae70105c5ca5f6f7e751"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_d5hfy1sixglt_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh pr list --repo openclaw/openclaw --search \"56220\" --state all --json number,t