{"type":"message","id":"9d92f47b","parentId":"4b162190","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:18:00.234Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"#56280 was closed and replaced by #56241. So the fix exists. Let me look at what #56241 actually changed - it added tests. Let me understand the actual bug.\n\nActually, let me look at this more carefully. The bug says \"Config validation rejects messages.tts.edge\" but the types.tts.ts shows `edge?: {...}`. So the types are fine, the schema should be fine. Unless... maybe the issue is that the path `messages.tts` doesn't actually exist in the schema?\n\nLet me check where `messages.tts` would be configured. Looking at the `MessagesSchema`, it has a `tts` field of type `TtsConfigSchema`. \n\nSo `messages.tts` is valid in the schema, and `TtsConfigSchema` includes the `edge` field. But if `messages.tts.edge` is being rejected, maybe the problem is that `messages` itself isn't where TTS config should go - perhaps it needs to be at the top level instead.\n\nLet me trace through the actual schema files to see where TTS configuration is really defined. I should look at `zod-schema.session.ts` and `zod-schema.providers-core.ts` to understand the correct configuration path, since the user mentioned the schema rejects `messages.tts.edge` despite the docs saying it's supported.\n\nActually, this is getting too deep into the weeds. The PR #56241 is already being worked on and adding tests, so I should let that move forward rather than keep digging into the schema details. Instead, let me scan through recent commits to see if there are any obvious bugs I can fix.","thinkingSignature":"60511561de6beed638f290f02b0908a0a1a43716af2c189013efa08a4c21a603"},{"type":"text","text":"好，#56241 已经有人修并加了测试。我来快速验证一下这个 PR 的测试是否充分。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5uhhbrf9rhm6_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/pulls/56241/files --jq '.[] | {filename:.filename,adds:.additions,dels:.d