{"type":"message","id":"7e751cb5","parentId":"d53aa130","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:18:29.439Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no reference to `messages.tts` in the schema files. So the path `messages.tts.edge` doesn't exist in the schema. That means if someone configures `messages.tts.edge` in their `openclaw.json`, it would be rejected as an unknown key (because of `.strict()`).\n\nBut the types say it's supported... Let me look at the actual issue description again.\n\nActually wait - the issue title says \"Config schema rejects legacy messages.tts.edge while docs/types still say it is supported\". This means someone is using `messages.tts.edge` in their config and it gets rejected by the strict schema, but the TypeScript types indicate it should be valid. \n\nSo the PR adds tests to verify that the schema accepts `messages.tts.edge`, even though the schema doesn't actually have this path defined yet. This suggests the fix might involve actually adding `messages.tts.edge` as a valid configuration option in the schema, not just documenting that it should work.\n\nBut wait - if the tests pass after adding them, that means the schema is already accepting `messages.tts.edge`. So either the schema already has this path somewhere, or the tests are validating something that already works. I need to look at what these new tests are actually checking to understand the current state.","thinkingSignature":"69faaba4edde666ea08c9bae64c03cbb2e2bb1d633ea86a61a6932284634c36d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_f1z3pk0gr5rp_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/openclaw-fork/src/config/zod-schema.tts.test.ts | tail -50"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79965,"output":307,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":102897,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703893230,"responseId":"061