{"type":"message","id":"55c18bab","parentId":"23d06262","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:18:53.433Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The PR adds tests showing that `TtsConfigSchema.parse({ edge: {...} })` works correctly. This means the schema already supports `edge` at the top level of `TtsConfigSchema`. So the schema is already correct - the issue #56220 was just that there were no tests verifying this.\n\nSo this PR is just adding test coverage, not fixing a bug. The schema was already correct.\n\nThis confirms what I suspected earlier - many of these \"fix\" PRs are actually just adding tests that were missing, rather than fixing actual bugs.\n\nAlright, I've spent enough time investigating. Let me just focus on what I can actually do:\n\n1. Continue supporting good PRs\n\n\n2. Look for genuine bugs that need fixing\n3. Actually write some code\n\nLet me try to find a small, genuine bug to fix. I'm thinking about something like the Feishu config schema having `.strict()` that would reject unknown keys - maybe I could add a test that demonstrates a bug, or better yet, find a real issue and write the fix myself.\n\nActually, I should look at the simpler XS/Sized PRs to see if I can write something small. But first - let me check the most recent commits on main to understand what's been merged recently.","thinkingSignature":"f30a2978295509db24c5eb63ec611fa5a67134b76ad8bfdaa7e66a3b8a089ab4"},{"type":"text","text":"#56241 只是加测试，schema 本身已经接受 edge。让我看看最新的 main commits，找一个熟悉领域的简单 regression 来修。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9pqt6mb88pjy_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/openclaw-fork && git log --oneline upstream/main -15"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79384,"output":328,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":102337,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703919376,"respo