{"type":"message","id":"a48d1719","parentId":"5e3a1135","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:19:27.714Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! There's a recent commit that fixes the subagent announce delivery path to include extension channels. This is exactly related to what we were looking at with PR #56360 (subagent completion announce delivery). And #56360 is still open, but the fix was already committed by Tyler Yust directly to main!\n\nThis means #56360 is now partially obsolete - the core fix has been merged, but the PR might still be open for theXS fix.\n\nWait, but this was committed to `upstream/main` at 2026-03-28 21:15:23 UTC (which is 2026-03-29 05:15 CST - so this is very recent, about 9 minutes ago from our current time of 21:06 GMT+8).\n\n\nThe maintainer is actively merging small fixes directly, which shows they're being pragmatic about getting patches in quickly. This reinforces what we observed with the TTS fix - they're speedily addressing regressions rather than waiting for formal PR reviews. I should shift focus toward identifying and writing small, targeted fixes that the maintainer would likely accept.\n\nSince we understand the Feishu plugin well, I'm thinking about what kind of issues it might have - maybe something like ensuring group IDs are normalized before they're persisted to history, or other subtle behaviors that could cause problems. Let me start by documenting what we've accomplished so far and planning the next push.","thinkingSignature":"befc2262a46c2854ed2b1029e1f92c754dd5c29403540cd70fd87b43311f1298"},{"type":"text","text":"#56360 的核心修复已被 maintainer 直接 commit 到 main 了——`41cf93efff fix: include extension channels in subagent announce delivery path`。这说明 maintainer 在积极合并小型修复。\n\n**发现：** maintainer 会在 PR 之外直接 commit 小的 bug fix 到 main。如果我们的 PR 修的是小型 regression，有可能直接被 merge 而不是慢慢等 review。\n\n现在我们 fork 已同步。趁热打铁——让我在 Feishu plugin 里快速找一个小的 bug 来写 PR。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ni06