{"type":"message","id":"8701d9e9","parentId":"aca05eeb","timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:19:58.879Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No 401 token refresh logic in the Feishu plugin. The issue description says the 401 happens in the pi-ai layer (model API), not in the Feishu channel itself. The Feishu embedded agent calls the model API, gets a 401, and surfaces it to the user instead of refreshing the token.\n\nThis is a more complex issue that involves the pi-ai integration, not just the Feishu plugin. Let me look at this more carefully.\n\nActually, let me just accept that writing a PR from scratch is going to take more time than I have right now. Let me instead focus on what I can do quickly:1. Continue to support good PRs\n2. Try to write a VERY small doc or test fix\n\n\n3. Push our fork and make sure it's up to date\n\nActually, I should just push our fork to origin first - we've rebased to upstream/main and it's clean, so let's get it synced.","thinkingSignature":"e855f7ffe813968204037656a37ddc59b6321dfb5aae6d60ea458b6cea3ba9fc"},{"type":"text","text":"好，找 bug 写 PR 的难度比预期高——大部分要么已被修，要么太深。让我先把 fork 推到 origin 保持同步，然后继续支持 PR。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_kjxtu9fjde3f_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/openclaw-fork && git push origin main 2>&1","yieldMs":30000,"timeout":60}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":79186,"output":293,"cacheRead":22625,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":102104,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774703989441,"responseId":"06170875778232037d0541e11ebedb28"}}
