erprets them through the old parameter names—`isDirectMessage` maps correctly, but `cfg` gets treated as `globalConfig` and `accountId` as `groupConfig`, completely breaking the logic.\\n\\n6. The issue is that TypeScript allows this mismatch at runtime since it erases types, so the function just silently uses the wrong variables and returns incorrect results.\\n\\n7. I need to check whether the upstream/openclaw main branch has already resolved this bug, since that would determine if I should fix it there or in my fork.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n              \"id\": \"call_function_ctiav0zj98k6_1\",\n              \"name\": \"exec\",\n              \"arguments\": {\n                \"command\": \"cd /root/.openclaw/workspaces/workspace-lingling/openclaw-fork && git log --oneline upstream/main | grep \\\"56338\\\\|requireMention\\\\|feishu.*mention\\\" | head -10\",\n                \"timeout\": 15\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n          \"provider\": \"minimax\",\n          \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7\",\n          \"usage\": {\n            \"input\": 55259,\n            \"output\": 364,\n            \"totalTokens\": 71013,\n            \"cacheRead\": 15390,\n            \"cacheWrite\": 0,\n            \"cost\": {\n              \"total\": 0\n            }\n          },\n          \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n          \"timestamp\": 1774702404701,\n          \"responseId\": \"06170244a7827eb45d583653106776d3\",\n          \"__openclaw\": {\n            \"id\": \"ade1723f\",\n            \"seq\": 441\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"agent:main:feishu:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n      \"kind\": \"other\",\n      \"channel\": \"webchat\",\n      \"displayName\": \"webchat:g-agent-main-feishu-feishu-default-direct-ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n      \"deliveryContext\": {\n        \"cha